- [Tom] For what?

262
00:08:33,833 --> 00:08:36,600
(imitating song)

263
00:08:37,600 --> 00:08:38,533
- I can't believe you.

264
00:08:38,533 --> 00:08:39,733
- [Tom] I can't understand you.

265
00:08:39,733 --> 00:08:40,967
- I started ten
minutes before you.

266
00:08:40,967 --> 00:08:42,100
And you're not even winded.

267
00:08:42,100 --> 00:08:42,933
- I'm winded.

268
00:08:42,933 --> 00:08:43,767
- From driving.

269
00:08:43,767 --> 00:08:44,733
- You hide it well.

270
00:08:44,733 --> 00:08:46,267
I'm having a heart attack.

271
00:08:46,267 --> 00:08:47,933
- Lower the heart rate.

272
00:08:47,933 --> 00:08:49,800
Drop the respiration.

273
00:08:49,800 --> 00:08:51,100
Slow everything down.

274
00:08:51,100 --> 00:08:52,833
- [Tom] Make good money at home.

275
00:08:52,833 --> 00:08:54,900
- I thought I was in
shape, till I met you.

276
00:08:54,900 --> 00:08:56,333
- [Trainer] It'll come.

277
00:08:56,333 --> 00:08:57,233
- A heart attack?

278
00:08:57,233 --> 00:08:58,667
Any second.

279
00:08:58,667 --> 00:09:00,600
- When you have to run the
four-minute mile, you'll do it.

280
00:09:00,600 --> 00:09:02,600
- [Tom] You'll be a
Henson rat, like me.

281
00:09:02,600 --> 00:09:04,367
- I don't think
running's my long suit.

282
00:09:04,367 --> 00:09:05,767
I'll stick to wheels.

283
00:09:05,767 --> 00:09:07,400
At least you don't ride bikes.

284
00:09:07,400 --> 00:09:08,800
- Doodly doodly doodly.

285
00:09:08,800 --> 00:09:10,533
I can't believe
I'm riding a bike!

286
00:09:10,533 --> 00:09:12,500
- It's been a long time.

287
00:09:12,500 --> 00:09:14,100
- Since I rock and rolled?

288
00:09:14,100 --> 00:09:15,633
- Get ready to watch
the A's, old fella?

289
00:09:15,633 --> 00:09:16,467
- [Joel] Huh?

290
00:09:16,467 --> 00:09:17,300
- [Tom] What?

291
00:09:17,300 --> 00:09:19,033
(laughing)

292
00:09:19,033 --> 00:09:20,267
I love buddy films.

293
00:09:20,267 --> 00:09:21,667
This is just like
The Last Boy Scout.

294
00:09:21,667 --> 00:09:22,500
- [Joel] Really?

295
00:09:22,500 --> 00:09:25,100
(light synth music)

296
00:09:25,100 --> 00:09:27,733
- [Tom] It sounds like
Chicago Tansit Authority.

297
00:09:27,733 --> 00:09:31,000
(imitating horn music)

298
00:09:33,167 --> 00:09:34,133
- [Announcer] Good afternoon,
ladies and gentlemen.

299
00:09:34,133 --> 00:09:35,600
- Do not take the green acid.

300
00:09:35,600 --> 00:09:37,067
- [Tom] Whoo.

301
00:09:37,067 --> 00:09:38,333
- [Announcer] Clearwater
motocross championship race.

302
00:09:38,333 --> 00:09:39,867
- [Tom] Hey look, it's
Francis Ford Coppola.

303
00:09:39,867 --> 00:09:41,100
- [Announcer] Beautiful sunny
afternoon here at Clearwater.

304
00:09:41,100 --> 00:09:43,133
We'll have a great
day for racing.

305
00:09:43,133 --> 00:09:45,033
- So I come around the
last turn like I'm flying.

306
00:09:45,033 --> 00:09:46,667
Bam, right across
the finish line--

307
00:09:46,667 --> 00:09:47,600
- [Tom] Wait a minute.

308
00:09:47,600 --> 00:09:49,267
Where did he get that thing?

309
00:09:49,267 --> 00:09:50,800
- Look, I admire
your confidence.

310
00:09:50,800 --> 00:09:53,400
But it for some reason or
another, you should lose.

311
00:09:53,400 --> 00:09:54,967
- Easy money.

312
00:09:54,967 --> 00:09:56,933
Hang on to Henry
for me, will you?

313
00:09:56,933 --> 00:09:58,867
He loves the straightaways,
but he hates the turns.

314
00:09:58,867 --> 00:10:00,633
- [Joel] Anybody
catch what he said?

315
00:10:00,633 --> 00:10:02,233
- [Tom] Not a word.

316
00:10:03,833 --> 00:10:05,833
- [Announcer] We've got entrants
from all over the country.

317
00:10:05,833 --> 00:10:07,067
- [Joel] All over the world!

318
00:10:07,067 --> 00:10:08,000
- [Announcer] Max
Keller will be here,

319
00:10:08,000 --> 00:10:08,667
winner of last year's race.

320
00:10:08,667 --> 00:10:10,133
- [All] Boo.

321
00:10:10,133 --> 00:10:11,533
- [Announcer] Our own
Chad Webster, Bill Howard,

322
00:10:11,533 --> 00:10:14,300
and Carrie Brown,
representing the cannery.

323
00:10:14,300 --> 00:10:15,233
- Uh oh.

324
00:10:15,233 --> 00:10:16,333
Here come the no-goodniks.

325
00:10:16,333 --> 00:10:17,267
- [Tom] Yep.

326
00:10:17,267 --> 00:10:18,133
- [Joel] Why me?

327
00:10:18,133 --> 00:10:19,800
Why me all the time?

328
00:10:21,267 --> 00:10:22,200
- [Tom] Hey look,
it's Malcolm X.

329
00:10:22,200 --> 00:10:24,600
- [Joel] Oh, I don't think so.

330
00:10:27,100 --> 00:10:28,900
- Got a problem, pal?

331
00:10:28,900 --> 00:10:30,033
- Yeah, man.

332
00:10:30,033 --> 00:10:31,100
I don't like your face.

333
00:10:31,100 --> 00:10:32,433
- Yeah, well you're a jerk.

334
00:10:32,433 --> 00:10:33,367
- [Joel] Good one.

335
00:10:33,367 --> 00:10:34,333
- Wanna keep all those teeth?

336
00:10:34,333 --> 00:10:35,467
- Check out, Jack.

337
00:10:35,467 --> 00:10:36,300
- Max.

338
00:10:36,300 --> 00:10:37,133
- Stay out of this.

339
00:10:37,133 --> 00:10:38,033
I can handle it.

340
00:10:38,033 --> 00:10:39,567
- [Joel] It's Meat Loaf.

341
00:10:39,567 --> 00:10:43,200
- Rearranging that mug of
yours might be a challenge.

342
00:10:43,200 --> 00:10:44,667
- [Tom] D'oh.

343
00:10:44,667 --> 00:10:45,933
- Damn.

344
00:10:45,933 --> 00:10:48,200
I just injected him
with blowfish poison.

345
00:10:48,200 --> 00:10:49,400
- [Hog] Old Max Keller.

346
00:10:49,400 --> 00:10:50,100
- [Tom] Still
seeing that gerbil?

347
00:10:50,100 --> 00:10:50,933
- How you doing?

348
00:10:50,933 --> 00:10:51,900
Thought you retired.

349
00:10:51,900 --> 00:10:53,367
- I couldn't do that, brother.

350
00:10:53,367 --> 00:10:55,133
Besides, busting up
towns ain't cool anymore.

351
00:10:55,133 --> 00:10:57,133
- They must have gone to
speech, class together.

352
00:10:57,133 --> 00:10:58,367
- I would find you here.

353
00:10:58,367 --> 00:11:00,200
You any better with
that bike of yours now?

354
00:11:00,200 --> 00:11:02,333
- I always beat you, didn't I?

355
00:11:02,333 --> 00:11:04,767
Hey, Hog, this the
man, uh, McAllister.

356
00:11:04,767 --> 00:11:06,767
- [Joel] Uh, this is my
elderly gentleman friend.

357
00:11:06,767 --> 00:11:08,433
- Best biker around.

358
00:11:08,433 --> 00:11:09,767
- [Tom] My.

359
00:11:09,767 --> 00:11:10,967
So why do they call you Hog?

360
00:11:10,967 --> 00:11:12,333
- You better just watch.

361
00:11:12,333 --> 00:11:14,133
- [McAllister]
That's good advice.

362
00:11:14,133 --> 00:11:15,533
- Ebony at ivory.

363
00:11:17,933 --> 00:11:20,067
- [Tom] Hey, I got
walnuts in there.

364
00:11:20,067 --> 00:11:22,600
(engine revving)

365
00:11:22,600 --> 00:11:24,767
- [Joel] He's starting
up the guy's hand.

366
00:11:24,767 --> 00:11:26,633
- [Tom] That thing
hasn't worked in years.

367
00:11:26,633 --> 00:11:28,233
Thank you.

368
00:11:28,233 --> 00:11:29,600
- Good night.

369
00:11:29,600 --> 00:11:30,833
- Yeah, thanks.

370
00:11:30,833 --> 00:11:32,100
- See you later, Hog.

371
00:11:32,100 --> 00:11:33,967
- Uh, nice meeting
you, Mr. Pig, was it?

372
00:11:33,967 --> 00:11:35,100
Oh, Hog.

373
00:11:35,100 --> 00:11:35,933
That's it.

374
00:11:38,033 --> 00:11:39,467
- [Tom] Brrrrrrrm

375
00:11:40,933 --> 00:11:42,667
- Well, nice company you keep.

376
00:11:42,667 --> 00:11:44,300
- Ah, he's a pussycat.

377
00:11:44,300 --> 00:11:46,300
What'd you do to him anyway?

378
00:11:46,300 --> 00:11:47,833
- Oh, just being friendly.

379
00:11:47,833 --> 00:11:49,600
- Hope he can still
hold the handlebar.

380
00:11:49,600 --> 00:11:52,067
- Well, see you for the
champagne at the finish line.

381
00:11:52,067 --> 00:11:55,633
- [Joel] Um, pick up some
cedar chips for Muffy.

382
00:11:55,633 --> 00:11:58,167
- [Tom] Hey, easy
on the gerbil, Lee.

383
00:11:58,167 --> 00:11:59,400
Hey, whoa.

384
00:11:59,400 --> 00:12:00,533
- Things are not
what they seem, Lee.

385
00:12:00,533 --> 00:12:01,700
- [Announcer] Big crowd today.

386
00:12:01,700 --> 00:12:02,900
We appreciate that, folks.

387
00:12:02,900 --> 00:12:04,167
Always great to see you.

388
00:12:04,167 --> 00:12:06,067
- [Tom] Uh, believe me,
it's really a big crowd.

389
00:12:06,067 --> 00:12:07,833
- [Announcer] Going to be a
lot of fun out here today.

390
00:12:07,833 --> 00:12:10,833
You're going to see
some great bike racing.

391
00:12:10,833 --> 00:12:12,300
- Hi.

392
00:12:12,300 --> 00:12:13,933
- [Joel] Looks like the camera
lost interest in Timothy.

393
00:12:13,933 --> 00:12:15,433
- [Tom] I can see that.

394
00:12:15,433 --> 00:12:16,667
- What do you want?

395
00:12:16,667 --> 00:12:18,133
- Isn't that the kid
who won last year?

396
00:12:18,133 --> 00:12:19,967
- I don't remember.

397
00:12:19,967 --> 00:12:21,000
- [Joel] I know him

398
00:12:21,000 --> 00:12:22,100
- Well, tell him.

399
00:12:22,100 --> 00:12:23,800
I'm not interested.

400
00:12:23,800 --> 00:12:25,100
- You are so tough.

401
00:12:25,100 --> 00:12:26,600
- [Tom] Familiar.

402
00:12:26,600 --> 00:12:27,867
- You know, one of these
days, that mouth of yours

403
00:12:27,867 --> 00:12:29,533
is going to get you in
a lot of trouble. I--

404
00:12:29,533 --> 00:12:30,867
- And you what?

405
00:12:30,867 --> 00:12:32,767
Take a walk, Webster.

406
00:12:32,767 --> 00:12:34,000
- Listen, lady--

407
00:12:34,000 --> 00:12:35,500
- [Tom] It's on the
tip of my tongue.

408
00:12:35,500 --> 00:12:37,633
- This race track is one place
in this town you don't own.

409
00:12:37,633 --> 00:12:39,533
- [Tom] It's Scott Hamilton!

410
00:12:39,533 --> 00:12:41,033
That's who it is!

411
00:12:41,033 --> 00:12:43,100
- Out here, you've got to
beat me fair and square.

412
00:12:43,100 --> 00:12:45,233
- Ooh, she's a little spitfire.

413
00:12:45,233 --> 00:12:46,467
- [Tom] Grr.

414
00:12:46,467 --> 00:12:48,300
- Unless, of course,
you're too gutless

415
00:12:48,300 --> 00:12:50,567
to try without your daddy's
money to back you up.

416
00:12:50,567 --> 00:12:51,633
- [Tom] D'oh!

417
00:12:51,633 --> 00:12:52,833
Pearl drops.

418
00:12:52,833 --> 00:12:53,633
Mmm.

419
00:12:55,667 --> 00:12:57,900
(laughing)

420
00:13:00,700 --> 00:13:01,633
- It's a Ren Fest.

421
00:13:01,633 --> 00:13:02,900
- [Tom] Mmm.

422
00:13:02,900 --> 00:13:03,967
- [Announcer] Just
a few more seconds

423
00:13:03,967 --> 00:13:05,400
before the gun goes off.

424
00:13:05,400 --> 00:13:06,767
All jockeying for position.

425
00:13:06,767 --> 00:13:09,400
(imitating engine revving)

426
00:13:09,400 --> 00:13:11,400
- They all look so good.

427
00:13:14,167 --> 00:13:17,900
(imitating engine revving)

428
00:13:17,900 --> 00:13:18,700
- [Announcer] There's the gun.

429
00:13:18,700 --> 00:13:19,633
And they're off.

430
00:13:19,633 --> 00:13:21,967
- [All] Go Charlie Brown, go!

431
00:13:21,967 --> 00:13:23,567
- [Announcer] But Max
Keller is right behind him.

432
00:13:23,567 --> 00:13:25,700
And I can see Big Jim Stevenson.

433
00:13:25,700 --> 00:13:27,233
- [Tom] Big Jim Seaborn?

434
00:13:27,233 --> 00:13:28,267
- [Announcer] With friends.

435
00:13:28,267 --> 00:13:29,233
And enemies.

436
00:13:29,233 --> 00:13:30,700
Number 11.

437
00:13:30,700 --> 00:13:32,867
And there's Carrie Brown,
coming up fast on the inside.

438
00:13:32,867 --> 00:13:34,933
- And there's Linda Ronstadt
behind him on roller skates!

439
00:13:34,933 --> 00:13:36,133
- [Announcer] Uh oh.

440
00:13:36,133 --> 00:13:37,367
Uh oh, there's a pile-up.

441
00:13:37,367 --> 00:13:39,200
Doesn't look as
if anybody's hurt.

442
00:13:39,200 --> 00:13:41,433
- [Tom] Well, we
can dream, can't we?

443
00:13:41,433 --> 00:13:42,867
- [Announcer] Racing
can be pretty rough.

444
00:13:42,867 --> 00:13:43,967
- [Tom] Nice PA.

445
00:13:43,967 --> 00:13:46,533
- William Katt, Freddy Mercury.

446
00:13:50,000 --> 00:13:50,933
- [Tom] Oh.

447
00:13:52,367 --> 00:13:54,167
- [Announcer] Nine to ten
racers have pulled away now.

448
00:13:54,167 --> 00:13:56,233
They leave the pack
behind in a cloud of dust.

449
00:13:56,233 --> 00:13:57,933
It's going to be a close finish.

450
00:13:57,933 --> 00:13:59,433
- [Tom] Here's my favorite.

451
00:13:59,433 --> 00:14:02,133
- [Announcer] Carrie
Brown, still the leader.

452
00:14:02,133 --> 00:14:04,500
- [Joel] Nothing
like enjoying nature

453
00:14:04,500 --> 00:14:06,100
on a screaming crotch rocket.

454
00:14:06,100 --> 00:14:07,167
- [Tom] M-hm.

455
00:14:08,633 --> 00:14:09,567
- Oof.

456
00:14:09,567 --> 00:14:11,400
Looks like Tony Scott directed.

457
00:14:11,400 --> 00:14:14,467
(laughing)

458
00:14:14,467 --> 00:14:18,367
- [Tom] This week on
Then Came Bronson.

459
00:14:18,367 --> 00:14:21,767
(light electronic music)

460
00:14:24,433 --> 00:14:25,867
- [Announcer] Here they are!

461
00:14:25,867 --> 00:14:27,367
- [Tom] Hey, he's breaking
into somebody's van.

462
00:14:27,367 --> 00:14:29,933
- [Announcer] Max Keller and
Carrie Brown all the way.

463
00:14:29,933 --> 00:14:31,767
They cross the finish line.

464
00:14:31,767 --> 00:14:33,600
- [Tom] Here they come.

465
00:14:33,600 --> 00:14:34,433
Oof.

466
00:14:34,433 --> 00:14:35,267
- Oh!

467
00:14:35,267 --> 00:14:36,400
Human speedbump.

468
00:14:36,400 --> 00:14:37,400
- [Tom] Ooh.

469
00:14:38,800 --> 00:14:40,700
- [Man] Hey, you all right?
What's the matter with that guy?

470
00:14:40,700 --> 00:14:41,633
- [Woman] I'm alive.

471
00:14:41,633 --> 00:14:43,100
- [Tom] She lives, she lives!

472
00:14:43,100 --> 00:14:43,933
Hoo-hoo!

473
00:14:47,200 --> 00:14:48,033
Yay.

474
00:14:49,167 --> 00:14:51,033
(crowd clapping)

475
00:14:51,033 --> 00:14:52,600
- [Joel] Max, I
lost the hamster.

476
00:14:52,600 --> 00:14:53,433
- Is she okay?

477
00:14:53,433 --> 00:14:54,567
- Okay?

478
00:14:54,567 --> 00:14:55,700
Yeah, she's okay.

479
00:14:55,700 --> 00:14:56,800
She won the race.

480
00:14:56,800 --> 00:14:58,267
- Even Ali lost a few.

481
00:14:58,267 --> 00:15:00,667
- Yeah, but never to a
girl with a shag haircut.

482
00:15:00,667 --> 00:15:02,067
Well, okay, once.

483
00:15:03,633 --> 00:15:05,233
- Thanks!

484
00:15:05,233 --> 00:15:06,100
- Nice race.

485
00:15:06,100 --> 00:15:07,433
Never lost it before.

486
00:15:07,433 --> 00:15:08,633
- Can I carry your bike home?

487
00:15:08,633 --> 00:15:09,467
- Well, I have.

488
00:15:09,467 --> 00:15:10,600
- Shame about your bike.

489
00:15:10,600 --> 00:15:12,067
Guys play rough around here.

490
00:15:12,067 --> 00:15:13,467
- Yeah, I know.

491
00:15:13,467 --> 00:15:15,000
You're pretty good.

492
00:15:15,000 --> 00:15:16,367
You almost beat me.

493
00:15:16,367 --> 00:15:17,233
- [Tom] D'oh!

494
00:15:17,233 --> 00:15:18,500
- That was the idea.

495
00:15:18,500 --> 00:15:20,233
- So, uh, how about a
little victory party?

496
00:15:20,233 --> 00:15:21,500
- [Tom] I got a gerbil.

497
00:15:21,500 --> 00:15:23,033
- [Max] At least dinner.

498
00:15:23,033 --> 00:15:26,700
- Well, um, I have to work
the early shift tomorrow.

499
00:15:26,700 --> 00:15:28,767
And I don't even know you.

500
00:15:28,767 --> 00:15:30,000
- [Joel] So okay.

501
00:15:30,000 --> 00:15:31,367
- You don't have
to buy me dinner.

502
00:15:31,367 --> 00:15:33,267
- I was thinking you might buy.

503
00:15:33,267 --> 00:15:34,100
- Oh.

504
00:15:34,100 --> 00:15:35,333
- [Tom] Ooh.

505
00:15:35,333 --> 00:15:36,300
- I mean, you won
all my prize money.

506
00:15:36,300 --> 00:15:38,200
- I'll think it over.

507
00:15:38,200 --> 00:15:41,267
- Uh, gee, that could
have gone better.

508
00:15:41,267 --> 00:15:43,600
Well, I didn't want her anyway.

509
00:15:43,600 --> 00:15:45,400
- I'm not used to seeing
them walk away from you.

510
00:15:45,400 --> 00:15:46,867
- [Tom] Usually
they run, screaming.

511
00:15:46,867 --> 00:15:48,700
- Lose one, you lose another.

512
00:15:48,700 --> 00:15:49,933
- [Tom] D'oh.

513
00:15:49,933 --> 00:15:51,233
- Good looking girl,
though, isn't she?

514
00:15:51,233 --> 00:15:53,133
Or does your ninja discipline

515
00:15:53,133 --> 00:15:54,667
make you immune to such things?

516
00:15:54,667 --> 00:15:57,133
- There are certain yearnings
one does not want to overcome.

517
00:15:57,133 --> 00:15:58,800
- [Tom] Besides, I
took a shuriken wheel

518
00:15:58,800 --> 00:15:59,733
in the whipper, once.

519
00:15:59,733 --> 00:16:00,600
- Ow.

520
00:16:01,567 --> 00:16:02,400
- [Max] Come on, Boss.

521
00:16:02,400 --> 00:16:04,600
(light jazz music)

522
00:16:04,600 --> 00:16:07,833
- Oh, is there going
to be a boat race?

523
00:16:09,200 --> 00:16:10,833
- [Tom] It's a secret
meeting of all those people

524
00:16:10,833 --> 00:16:12,400
who want this show canceled.

525
00:16:12,400 --> 00:16:14,233
- [Carrie] Oh, grab
a leaflet, please.

526
00:16:14,233 --> 00:16:16,600
- [Joel] F.I.S.T. with
Sylvester Stallone.

527
00:16:16,600 --> 00:16:18,467
- [Carrie] Grab a
leaflet, please.

528
00:16:18,467 --> 00:16:20,167
Union meeting tomorrow.

529
00:16:20,167 --> 00:16:21,367
Don't forget.

530
00:16:21,367 --> 00:16:22,900
- Oh, uh, it's a
Clifford Odets play.

531
00:16:22,900 --> 00:16:24,400
- [Joel] No, a Tom Bodett play.

532
00:16:24,400 --> 00:16:25,500
- Oh.

533
00:16:25,500 --> 00:16:26,333
Huh?

534
00:16:26,333 --> 00:16:27,267
- [Joel] Hey.

535
00:16:27,267 --> 00:16:28,133
- Still at it, huh, Carrie?

536
00:16:28,133 --> 00:16:29,900
- I don't quit, Harold.

537
00:16:29,900 --> 00:16:30,767
- [Tom] Ossie Davis?

538
00:16:30,767 --> 00:16:32,267
- Here, have a leaflet.

539
00:16:32,267 --> 00:16:34,233
- [Joel] Hey,
Pippi Longstocking.

540
00:16:34,233 --> 00:16:35,067
- Another meeting?

541
00:16:35,067 --> 00:16:35,900
- You bet.

542
00:16:35,900 --> 00:16:37,000
Tomorrow afternoon.

543
00:16:37,000 --> 00:16:39,733
And we're counting on you, Amy.

544
00:16:39,733 --> 00:16:41,967
We just need a few
more signatures.

545
00:16:41,967 --> 00:16:43,500
- Sure, sure.

546
00:16:43,500 --> 00:16:44,767
- When are you going to let
me take you dancing, Carrie?

547
00:16:44,767 --> 00:16:46,700
- When Welcome Back
Kotter is canceled.

548
00:16:46,700 --> 00:16:48,133
(laughing)

549
00:16:48,133 --> 00:16:49,600
- You sign this petition,
we'll talk about it.

550
00:16:49,600 --> 00:16:50,600
- All right.

551
00:16:50,600 --> 00:16:52,833
(laughing)

552
00:16:55,700 --> 00:16:57,167
- [Tom] Come on, Max.

553
00:16:57,167 --> 00:17:01,533
I know she rejected you,
but we've got to try again.

554
00:17:02,267 --> 00:17:03,067
- Well, this is it.

555
00:17:03,067 --> 00:17:04,400
Clearwater cannery.

556
00:17:04,400 --> 00:17:05,667
- Sure is dirty.

557
00:17:05,667 --> 00:17:09,667
- [Man] Nerve center of
the city, such as it is.

558
00:17:09,667 --> 00:17:11,033
- [Worker] Bring it over here.

559
00:17:11,033 --> 00:17:14,167
- [Tom] Hey don't
you ever say please?

560
00:17:14,167 --> 00:17:16,067
- You know, if I
hadn't lost that race,

561
00:17:16,067 --> 00:17:18,233
we wouldn't be broke.

562
00:17:18,233 --> 00:17:19,167
- Max.

563
00:17:19,167 --> 00:17:21,233
(suspenseful orchestral music)

564
00:17:21,233 --> 00:17:23,300
- So I figured I could pick
up a couple of days work here

565
00:17:23,300 --> 00:17:24,933
and put us back on schedule.

566
00:17:24,933 --> 00:17:25,867
- Max.

567
00:17:25,867 --> 00:17:26,800
- [Tom] Don't we know that box?

568
00:17:26,800 --> 00:17:28,667
- [Worker] Bring it down.

569
00:17:29,833 --> 00:17:31,833
- That does it, Flintstone!

570
00:17:31,833 --> 00:17:34,900
- [Joel] Right on
my head, that's it.

571
00:17:36,667 --> 00:17:37,567
- [Man] No!

572
00:17:40,333 --> 00:17:41,633
- [Tom] I think they
may just be too dumb

573
00:17:41,633 --> 00:17:42,900
to organize a union.

574
00:17:42,900 --> 00:17:44,733
- [Joel] Yeah.

575
00:17:44,733 --> 00:17:47,167
- Who killed my sister?

576
00:17:47,167 --> 00:17:48,400
Hee hee hee.

577
00:17:48,400 --> 00:17:50,833
- [Joel] Sorry,
it's my first day.

578
00:17:54,633 --> 00:17:56,267
- [Tom] Let's see.

579
00:17:56,267 --> 00:17:58,700
Won this in the claw machine
at the carnival. That'll work.

580
00:18:00,667 --> 00:18:03,033
- The right tool for
the right job, Lee.

581
00:18:03,033 --> 00:18:04,467
- [Tom] Stan Lee.

582
00:18:10,600 --> 00:18:12,100
Oh, my rheumatism.

583
00:18:14,700 --> 00:18:17,000
- [Joel] Oh, excellent,
Master Dipstick.

584
00:18:17,000 --> 00:18:20,400
That's $50,000 worth
of merchandise, Lee.

585
00:18:23,600 --> 00:18:25,700
- Listen, thanks a lot for
your help. I appreciate it.

586
00:18:25,700 --> 00:18:26,933
- Oh, forget it.

587
00:18:26,933 --> 00:18:28,467
When'd they issue this
equipment they're using?

588
00:18:28,467 --> 00:18:29,500
During the Depression?

589
00:18:29,500 --> 00:18:30,433
- Ha ha.

590
00:18:30,433 --> 00:18:31,433
It's great we can joke about it

591
00:18:31,433 --> 00:18:32,433
now that his hips are crushed.

592
00:18:32,433 --> 00:18:35,167
- It's not in their interests.

593
00:18:35,167 --> 00:18:36,267
- [Tom] Ahh!

594
00:18:36,267 --> 00:18:37,767
Don't move me off!

595
00:18:39,133 --> 00:18:41,967
(screaming)

596
00:18:41,967 --> 00:18:43,900
- Hey, it's Chico Marx.

597
00:18:45,833 --> 00:18:47,633
- [Joel] Hey, there's Lucy.

598
00:18:47,633 --> 00:18:49,233
- Ah, Ricky, I got ptomaine.

599
00:18:49,233 --> 00:18:50,867
Ahh.

600
00:18:50,867 --> 00:18:52,200
- Everybody works here.

601
00:18:52,200 --> 00:18:53,600
- [Tom] Does the
President work here?

602
00:18:53,600 --> 00:18:55,300
- Dinner tonight?

603
00:18:55,300 --> 00:18:56,800
- Okay.

604
00:18:56,800 --> 00:18:59,867
Um, why don't you meet me
at the Seaside Shanty--

605
00:18:59,867 --> 00:19:01,600
- What are these,
tongue-twisters?

606
00:19:01,600 --> 00:19:03,167
Are you making fun of me?

607
00:19:03,167 --> 00:19:04,867
- Do you think you can find it?

608
00:19:04,867 --> 00:19:06,000
- [Tom] Heh heh.

609
00:19:06,000 --> 00:19:07,767
- I'll see you later.

610
00:19:09,967 --> 00:19:11,600
- [Tom] Wilford
Brimley, safecracker.

611
00:19:11,600 --> 00:19:14,200
- Did they tell you
what happened out there?

612
00:19:14,200 --> 00:19:16,833
You nearly got Joe
Henderson killed.

613
00:19:16,833 --> 00:19:17,700
- [Tom] You!

614
00:19:17,700 --> 00:19:18,700
- Rotting equipment.

615
00:19:18,700 --> 00:19:19,533
- Now, Carrie--

616
00:19:19,533 --> 00:19:20,500
- Yeah, now's right.

617
00:19:20,500 --> 00:19:22,600
Now we're going to do something.

618
00:19:22,600 --> 00:19:23,667
- [Tom] I am the Walrus.

619
00:19:23,667 --> 00:19:24,533
Uh, I think.

620
00:19:24,533 --> 00:19:25,400
Yeah.

621
00:19:25,400 --> 00:19:26,633
- He's too old.

622
00:19:26,633 --> 00:19:28,467
There are plenty of
other jobs he can do.

623
00:19:28,467 --> 00:19:29,500
Not that one.

624
00:19:29,500 --> 00:19:30,933
- [Tom] Look, his chin's acting.

625
00:19:30,933 --> 00:19:32,067
- What has to happen
around here before someone

626
00:19:32,067 --> 00:19:33,767
takes an interest.

627
00:19:33,767 --> 00:19:35,167
When we get a union--

628
00:19:35,167 --> 00:19:36,400
- I told you.

629
00:19:36,400 --> 00:19:38,267
You'd better drop
that union talk.

630
00:19:38,267 --> 00:19:41,000
It's just going to get you
more trouble than you want.

631
00:19:41,000 --> 00:19:42,367
- Like it did my brother?

632
00:19:42,367 --> 00:19:43,800
- [Tom] Oh, sorry.

633
00:19:43,800 --> 00:19:45,100
My heart blew up again.

634
00:19:45,100 --> 00:19:46,667
- Done in by the cannery.

635
00:19:46,667 --> 00:19:48,000
Grow up, Carrie.

636
00:19:49,033 --> 00:19:49,867
- Dad?

637
00:19:49,867 --> 00:19:50,833
Uh, oh.

638
00:19:50,833 --> 00:19:51,667
- He split.

639
00:19:51,667 --> 00:19:52,633
- Another guy.

640
00:19:52,633 --> 00:19:54,833
- No more, no less.

641
00:19:54,833 --> 00:19:56,033
What'd you expect?

642
00:19:56,033 --> 00:19:57,967
The doctor get working
on the line here?

643
00:19:57,967 --> 00:19:59,700
- Well, I remember when you
were working on the line.

644
00:19:59,700 --> 00:20:01,633
So don't play that with
me. You're not that smart.

645
00:20:01,633 --> 00:20:02,800
But I am.

646
00:20:02,800 --> 00:20:04,033
- [Tom] Who?

647
00:20:04,033 --> 00:20:06,133
- And most of them's
going on around here.

648
00:20:06,133 --> 00:20:07,967
And when I found out what it is,

649
00:20:07,967 --> 00:20:11,400
I bet it's going to lead
me right back here to you.

650
00:20:11,400 --> 00:20:13,333
- She's got a Landers
Sister quality.

651
00:20:13,333 --> 00:20:14,567
- [Joel] Mm-hm.

652
00:20:14,567 --> 00:20:17,533
- [Tom] Don't even
think about it.

653
00:20:17,533 --> 00:20:20,633
- [Joel] Guess she won't
get her Christmas ham.

654
00:20:20,633 --> 00:20:22,600
- We are not putting
up with this.

655
00:20:22,600 --> 00:20:24,833
This is the most ridiculous
thing I have ever heard.

656
00:20:24,833 --> 00:20:26,667
- Ralph, I told you before,
I want that girl fired.

657
00:20:26,667 --> 00:20:28,833
- You think I don't
want her out of my hair?

658
00:20:28,833 --> 00:20:30,133
You listen to me, Chad Webster.

659
00:20:30,133 --> 00:20:31,633
You've got a couple
of things to learn

660
00:20:31,633 --> 00:20:32,567
about running this cannery.

661
00:20:32,567 --> 00:20:34,033
(burping)

662
00:20:34,033 --> 00:20:35,300
And since your dad ain't
around to tell you, I will.

663
00:20:35,300 --> 00:20:37,700
We fire Kerry Brown, and
you won't get anybody

664
00:20:37,700 --> 00:20:38,967
in this town to work here.

665
00:20:38,967 --> 00:20:39,800
Nobody!

666
00:20:39,800 --> 00:20:41,300
They love that girl.

667
00:20:41,300 --> 00:20:42,500
- I'm telling you, the next
time she causes trouble.

668
00:20:42,500 --> 00:20:44,300
The very next time.

669
00:20:44,300 --> 00:20:46,500
- [Joel] Bet I
could eat that guy.

670
00:20:46,500 --> 00:20:47,700
Yep, I know it.

671
00:20:47,700 --> 00:20:48,867
Positive.

672
00:20:48,867 --> 00:20:49,833
- All right.

673
00:20:49,833 --> 00:20:50,967
No-Tell Motel.

674
00:20:52,733 --> 00:20:53,600
- Good looking, too.

675
00:20:53,600 --> 00:20:54,567
- [Tom] Hey, look.

676
00:20:54,567 --> 00:20:55,833
He's shaving his one hair.

677
00:20:55,833 --> 00:20:56,800
- You sure took care
of that accident down

678
00:20:56,800 --> 00:20:58,100
by the wharf today, didn't you?

679
00:20:58,100 --> 00:20:59,133
- [Joel] I think he cut
through his vocal cords

680
00:20:59,133 --> 00:20:59,967
or something.

681
00:20:59,967 --> 00:21:01,167
Sounds like it.

682
00:21:01,167 --> 00:21:02,367
- Just flip that
little gadget, and bam!

683
00:21:02,367 --> 00:21:03,733
The whole thing
goes into the drink.

684
00:21:03,733 --> 00:21:05,800
- Boy, that Gideon
writes a good novel.

685
00:21:05,800 --> 00:21:08,867
(light string music)

686
00:21:10,067 --> 00:21:14,367
- [Tom] I'm the floor in
an adult movie theater.

687
00:21:14,367 --> 00:21:15,300
- An older guy
like that shouldn't

688
00:21:15,300 --> 00:21:18,333
have to work that hard labor.

689
00:21:18,333 --> 00:21:20,767
- What, did Lee snap a
cyanide capsule in his mouth?

690
00:21:20,767 --> 00:21:22,333
- Centuries, right?

691
00:21:24,133 --> 00:21:26,300
So, say, what time is it?

692
00:21:26,300 --> 00:21:29,733
- [Joel] Can I wear
some of your clothes?

693
00:21:29,733 --> 00:21:30,800
I am so fine.

694
00:21:31,967 --> 00:21:33,100
- What's the matter?

695
00:21:33,100 --> 00:21:35,533
The bed too comfortable for you?

696
00:21:35,533 --> 00:21:36,767
You all right?

697
00:21:36,767 --> 00:21:38,000
Dear God, don't do this.

698
00:21:38,000 --> 00:21:40,567
- Hey, sounds like
a Resusci-Annie.

699
00:21:40,567 --> 00:21:43,200
- [Tom] Looks like a Resu--

700
00:21:43,200 --> 00:21:44,633
- Whatever happened to--

701
00:21:44,633 --> 00:21:45,733
- [Joel] Baby Jane?

702
00:21:45,733 --> 00:21:47,200
- It's time to get up?

703
00:21:47,200 --> 00:21:48,600
- What happened to you? I
thought you had a heart attack.

704
00:21:48,600 --> 00:21:50,100
- I was still.

705
00:21:50,100 --> 00:21:51,900
- You stopped breathing.

706
00:21:51,900 --> 00:21:53,333
You have to breathe.

707
00:21:53,333 --> 00:21:56,033
- The heartbeat, like everything
else, can be controlled.

708
00:21:56,033 --> 00:21:57,533
I just slowed it down.

709
00:21:57,533 --> 00:21:58,733
- Slowed it down?

710
00:21:58,733 --> 00:21:59,700
You stopped it.

711
00:21:59,700 --> 00:22:00,867
- Go all the way, next time.

712
00:22:00,867 --> 00:22:02,300
- Only in appearance.

713
00:22:02,300 --> 00:22:06,100
The same technique that
allows a Zulu warrior to chase

714
00:22:06,100 --> 00:22:08,167
a running gazelle for 50 miles--

715
00:22:08,167 --> 00:22:09,400
- [Tom] On a pogo stick.

716
00:22:09,400 --> 00:22:11,500
- And still have the
strength for the kill.

717
00:22:11,500 --> 00:22:13,267
- Swell. I believe
you can do it, okay?

718
00:22:13,267 --> 00:22:15,333
Just don't do it again. You
scared the hell out of me.

719
00:22:15,333 --> 00:22:16,233
- [Tom] It's okay.

720
00:22:16,233 --> 00:22:17,700
- Ah, that was nice.

721
00:22:17,700 --> 00:22:19,467
- [Joel] We've got to go.

722
00:22:19,467 --> 00:22:20,800
This one stings.

723
00:22:20,800 --> 00:22:22,067
- I think I am.

724
00:22:38,067 --> 00:22:39,733
- Well, since today's
movie features

725
00:22:39,733 --> 00:22:44,733
Timothy Van Patten's rocking
custom van so predominantly

726
00:22:46,200 --> 00:22:47,400
in the movie, we thought it
would be fun for the robots

727
00:22:47,400 --> 00:22:49,867
to get some pens
and pencils and make

728
00:22:49,867 --> 00:22:52,467
their versions of their
favorite '70s machines, okay?

729
00:22:52,467 --> 00:22:54,367
(cheering)

730
00:22:54,367 --> 00:22:55,600
So this one's Gypsy.

731
00:22:55,600 --> 00:22:56,867
You want to tell
everybody about it?

732
00:22:56,867 --> 00:22:58,400
- This is mine.

733
00:22:58,400 --> 00:23:01,033
It has a mural of Voyage
to the Bottom of the Sea.

734
00:23:01,033 --> 00:23:02,633
- Hey Joel, looks like a
lunchbox you used to have.

735
00:23:02,633 --> 00:23:03,900
- [Tom] Yeah.

736
00:23:03,900 --> 00:23:05,700
- [Joel] Okay, you want
to show the inside, too?

737
00:23:05,700 --> 00:23:07,400
- [Gypsy] And on the inside

738
00:23:07,400 --> 00:23:10,133
are 150 Richard
Basehart ventriloquist

739
00:23:10,133 --> 00:23:12,233
dummies, stacked like cordwood.

740
00:23:12,233 --> 00:23:13,400
- [Tom] Shades of Jame Gumb.

741
00:23:13,400 --> 00:23:14,633
- Jeepers.

742
00:23:14,633 --> 00:23:16,567
Okay, well, this one
looks like yours, Tom.

743
00:23:16,567 --> 00:23:19,133
- Yeah, yeah, that's mine.
- Wanna tell them about it?

744
00:23:19,133 --> 00:23:20,733
- Well, the exterior
of my van would

745
00:23:20,733 --> 00:23:23,267
be based on the work of fantasy
illustrator Frank Frazetta,

746
00:23:23,267 --> 00:23:26,100
custom-painted at Vantastic
Studios in Lake Geneva,

747
00:23:26,100 --> 00:23:28,000
Wisconsin, and insured
for over $1,200.

748
00:23:28,000 --> 00:23:30,267
Then the interior,
show them the interior,

749
00:23:30,267 --> 00:23:31,733
it's really cool.

750
00:23:31,733 --> 00:23:33,300
It would be painted just like
the Sistine Chapel inside,

751
00:23:33,300 --> 00:23:34,833
only it'd be real
dirty, you know.

752
00:23:34,833 --> 00:23:37,200
Plus it'd have a waterbed
and a fireplace slash bar.

753
00:23:37,200 --> 00:23:39,100
And an in-dash lotion dispenser.

754
00:23:39,100 --> 00:23:40,333
And if I dented it up,

755
00:23:40,333 --> 00:23:41,600
I'd spend six weeks
in the shop class,

756
00:23:41,600 --> 00:23:43,167
or at Harv's Speed
Shop, that's what

757
00:23:43,167 --> 00:23:44,733
we used to call it
when I was there.

758
00:23:44,733 --> 00:23:46,033
And we'd just sand it
and put Bondo on it.

759
00:23:46,033 --> 00:23:47,767
And I wouldn't go to
any of the classes,

760
00:23:47,767 --> 00:23:49,833
and at lunch, Clem an I would
get in the, get in the van,

761
00:23:49,833 --> 00:23:52,000
leave campus, go downtown,
and have a beer at the Shire.

762
00:23:52,000 --> 00:23:52,900
Yeah, it would be really cool.

763
00:23:52,900 --> 00:23:54,167
Heh, whoo.

764
00:23:54,167 --> 00:23:56,267
- [Joel] Okay, and this
next one's, uh, Crow's.

765
00:23:56,267 --> 00:23:59,700
- [Crow] Well, my van would
have an ergonomically designed

766
00:23:59,700 --> 00:24:02,300
desk and chair, plus a shelf
for all my reference material.

767
00:24:02,300 --> 00:24:03,500
And my computer.

768
00:24:03,500 --> 00:24:05,200
And a good reliable
reading lamp.

769
00:24:05,200 --> 00:24:06,900
And I'd pack an extra
pair of glasses,

770
00:24:06,900 --> 00:24:08,933
and some sensible
shoes, and a cooler

771
00:24:08,933 --> 00:24:10,767
full of ice cold
Coke, Diet Coke,

772
00:24:10,767 --> 00:24:12,333
and ice cold mineral water.

773
00:24:12,333 --> 00:24:13,567
- [Joel] Uh huh.

774
00:24:13,567 --> 00:24:15,400
And what about the
exterior there?

775
00:24:15,400 --> 00:24:17,533
- [Crow] Uh, I'd
have Ed Big Daddy

776
00:24:17,533 --> 00:24:20,033
Don Roth do a mural of me
with my eyes popping out

777
00:24:20,033 --> 00:24:21,400
with my tongue dragging.

778
00:24:21,400 --> 00:24:23,667
And big old gnarled
hand on the giant stick

779
00:24:23,667 --> 00:24:25,333
shift putting in six.

780
00:24:25,333 --> 00:24:27,667
And the side of machine would
read like it was in blood,

781
00:24:27,667 --> 00:24:28,667
The Van Die.

782
00:24:29,800 --> 00:24:30,633
- Yeah!

783
00:24:30,633 --> 00:24:31,900
Whoo, yeah.

784
00:24:31,900 --> 00:24:33,133
- Oh, I don't think so.

785
00:24:33,133 --> 00:24:34,867
We've got Commercial Sign.

786
00:24:34,867 --> 00:24:38,300
(light electronic music)

787
00:24:40,467 --> 00:24:41,700
- [Max] So I found myself--

788
00:24:41,700 --> 00:24:43,267
- [Joel] It's Ed Big
Daddy Roth, Crow.

789
00:24:43,267 --> 00:24:44,533
- [Max] I've learned my lesson.

790
00:24:44,533 --> 00:24:47,700
Not leaving this bar
through the window.

791
00:24:48,900 --> 00:24:50,667
(whistling)

792
00:24:50,667 --> 00:24:52,200
- [Tom] That is one good
looking union organizer.

793
00:24:52,200 --> 00:24:53,033
- Hi, Sandy.

794
00:24:53,033 --> 00:24:53,867
- Hi.

795
00:24:55,500 --> 00:24:56,500
- Hey. Sandy.

796
00:24:56,500 --> 00:24:57,933
I don't want you serving Carrie.

797
00:24:57,933 --> 00:24:59,367
- Why not?

798
00:24:59,367 --> 00:25:00,900
- Because I said so. I
don't want you serving her.

799
00:25:00,900 --> 00:25:02,500
- Chad, what's the problem?
- Want to lose your job?

800
00:25:02,500 --> 00:25:03,333
Do what I told you.

801
00:25:03,333 --> 00:25:04,167
- Okay.

802
00:25:08,133 --> 00:25:09,267
- [Tom] Evening, everybody.

803
00:25:09,267 --> 00:25:10,467
- [All] Norm!

804
00:25:10,467 --> 00:25:12,133
- I thought you didn't drink.

805
00:25:12,133 --> 00:25:14,233
- I don't break
up dates, either.

806
00:25:14,233 --> 00:25:16,533
Unless she gets to
be too much for you.

807
00:25:16,533 --> 00:25:18,933
- That's brave talk from a man
whose heart almost stopped.

808
00:25:18,933 --> 00:25:19,900
- [Tom] It didn't stop.

809
00:25:19,900 --> 00:25:21,133
It slowed down.

810
00:25:22,267 --> 00:25:23,700
Hey, look on the wall.

811
00:25:23,700 --> 00:25:26,167
It's Milton Berle's
netted slingshot briefs.

812
00:25:26,167 --> 00:25:27,100
- I'm here.

813
00:25:28,200 --> 00:25:29,033
- Is this your card?

814
00:25:29,033 --> 00:25:30,500
- Yeah, I'm here.

815
00:25:30,500 --> 00:25:32,167
Oh, Max, a long day.

816
00:25:33,633 --> 00:25:34,633
- I hear ya.

817
00:25:35,533 --> 00:25:37,700
- [Joel] You're a wry wit.

818
00:25:39,400 --> 00:25:41,300
- [Tom] Aren't
these people phony?

819
00:25:41,300 --> 00:25:43,567
- You guys passing through?

820
00:25:45,000 --> 00:25:46,033
- You talking to me?

821
00:25:46,033 --> 00:25:47,833
- What's it look like?

822
00:25:47,833 --> 00:25:49,367
- [Joel] Well, you do
have that funny eye.

823
00:25:49,367 --> 00:25:50,900
- You and the hotshot
kid over there.

824
00:25:50,900 --> 00:25:53,367
Now that he's lost the race, I
guess you'll be leaving town.

825
00:25:53,367 --> 00:25:55,200
- What's it to you?

826
00:25:55,200 --> 00:25:56,433
- [Tom] Drives the plot.

827
00:25:56,433 --> 00:25:57,933
- Well, this is a
tight community.

828
00:25:57,933 --> 00:26:00,267
We take care of our town.

829
00:26:00,267 --> 00:26:03,133
- I don't think the lady
wants you to take care of her.

830
00:26:03,133 --> 00:26:05,400
- That's why the
lady is a tramp.

831
00:26:05,400 --> 00:26:08,233
- You got a hearing problem?

832
00:26:08,233 --> 00:26:09,767
- My hearing is excellent.

833
00:26:09,767 --> 00:26:11,400
- [Joel] Because I
have the Whisper 2000.

834
00:26:11,400 --> 00:26:12,900
- Move it or lose it.

835
00:26:12,900 --> 00:26:16,067
- [Tom] I haven't heard
that since grade school.

836
00:26:16,067 --> 00:26:18,000
- You just be sure lover boy
is on his way out of town.

837
00:26:18,000 --> 00:26:19,700
- [Tom] I love that band.
- [Joel] Yeah!

838
00:26:19,700 --> 00:26:21,133
- I'll deliver the message.

839
00:26:21,133 --> 00:26:22,300
- You do that.

840
00:26:23,500 --> 00:26:25,533
- Can I have a quarter?

841
00:26:25,533 --> 00:26:26,767
- You got a light?

842
00:26:26,767 --> 00:26:27,900
- [Tom] Yeah, my
butt and your fa--

843
00:26:27,900 --> 00:26:29,633
Oh, that's not right.

844
00:26:32,233 --> 00:26:33,067
Flame on!

845
00:26:34,933 --> 00:26:35,767
- Oh.

846
00:26:36,867 --> 00:26:39,333
Must've had it
turned up too high.

847
00:26:39,333 --> 00:26:40,567
- What is that?

848
00:26:40,567 --> 00:26:42,033
A cigarette lighter
or a flamethrower?

849
00:26:42,033 --> 00:26:45,667
- [Tom] It's a cigarette
lighter and a flamethrower.

850
00:26:47,067 --> 00:26:48,267
- Be seeing you.

851
00:26:48,267 --> 00:26:49,267
- Yeah, right.

852
00:26:49,267 --> 00:26:50,800
In all the old familiar places.

853
00:26:50,800 --> 00:26:51,633
- Uh, let's order.

854
00:26:51,633 --> 00:26:52,833
Is this still on you?

855
00:26:52,833 --> 00:26:53,667
- You bet.

856
00:26:54,633 --> 00:26:56,133
- See some menus, please?

857
00:26:56,133 --> 00:26:57,567
Sure.

858
00:26:57,567 --> 00:26:58,333
- [Tom] Can we have some
more lighting over here, too?

859
00:26:58,333 --> 00:26:59,267
- Excuse me.

860
00:26:59,267 --> 00:27:01,000
You didn't get the lady a menu.

861
00:27:01,000 --> 00:27:02,167
- I can't serve her.

862
00:27:02,167 --> 00:27:03,433
- Sandy.

863
00:27:03,433 --> 00:27:04,367
- What do you mean,
you can't serve her?

864
00:27:04,367 --> 00:27:05,300
- [Tom] She's off the menu.

865
00:27:05,300 --> 00:27:06,233
- Don't start any trouble.

866
00:27:06,233 --> 00:27:07,433
- Well, how about if I do?

867
00:27:07,433 --> 00:27:09,700
I just decided
dinner's on me tonight.

868
00:27:09,700 --> 00:27:10,567
- [Tom] Say!

869
00:27:10,567 --> 00:27:11,833
- And I'm really hungry.

870
00:27:11,833 --> 00:27:13,133
- [All] Hm. Come from a
long line of big eaters.

871
00:27:13,133 --> 00:27:14,700
Uh, you like seafood?

872
00:27:14,700 --> 00:27:15,533
- You bet.

873
00:27:15,533 --> 00:27:16,367
- [Max] Halibut?

874
00:27:16,367 --> 00:27:17,200
- Yeah.

875
00:27:17,200 --> 00:27:18,033
- Me too.

876
00:27:18,033 --> 00:27:19,533
- [Tom] Me too, seafood.

877
00:27:19,533 --> 00:27:20,800
- Two halibuts, I'm really
hungry. Two baked potatoes.

878
00:27:20,800 --> 00:27:22,200
- [Joel] Wow.
- [Max] Sour cream and chives?

879
00:27:22,200 --> 00:27:23,033
Only on one.

880
00:27:23,033 --> 00:27:23,867
- Yeah, Tim.

881
00:27:23,867 --> 00:27:24,700
Go, man.

882
00:27:24,700 --> 00:27:25,533
Order, buddy.

883
00:27:25,533 --> 00:27:27,000
Rave on.

884
00:27:27,000 --> 00:27:29,033
- And, um to finish it off,
I'll have a couple of apple pies

885
00:27:29,033 --> 00:27:30,167
with ice cream on the top.

886
00:27:30,167 --> 00:27:31,833
- Yeah!
- And a pot of coffee.

887
00:27:31,833 --> 00:27:33,200
That should just
about do me fine.

888
00:27:33,200 --> 00:27:34,433
- And, uh, two hard-boiled
eggs. (honking)

889
00:27:34,433 --> 00:27:35,200
Make that three
hard-boiled eggs.

890
00:27:35,200 --> 00:27:36,133
- Oh.

891
00:27:36,133 --> 00:27:37,067
Now you can't serve me either.

892
00:27:37,067 --> 00:27:39,533
- Look, Carrie, it's not me.

893
00:27:39,533 --> 00:27:40,400
- [Tom] Uh oh.

894
00:27:40,400 --> 00:27:41,333
It's Dave Lennox.

895
00:27:41,333 --> 00:27:42,600
- It looks like Annie Lennox.

896
00:27:42,600 --> 00:27:44,667
- [Man] Maybe you ought
to order someplace else.

897
00:27:44,667 --> 00:27:46,400
- Then I won't be
eating all of this.

898
00:27:46,400 --> 00:27:49,567
- [Joel] Uh, we have
busboys for that.

899
00:27:52,567 --> 00:27:53,900
- We're famous for our chops.

900
00:27:53,900 --> 00:27:55,700
- [Tom] Give me a breadbasket.

901
00:27:55,700 --> 00:27:56,533
- [Joel] Yeah?

902
00:27:56,533 --> 00:27:58,433
Well, how's your punch?

903
00:28:00,367 --> 00:28:03,600
- [Tom] Tim, this is for
the seafood lover in you.

904
00:28:03,600 --> 00:28:06,000
(screaming)

905
00:28:06,000 --> 00:28:07,567
- What a loser.

906
00:28:07,567 --> 00:28:09,667
- [Tom] Hm, what a loser.

907
00:28:11,000 --> 00:28:12,867
- I've got to break
myself of this habit.

908
00:28:12,867 --> 00:28:14,300
- [Tom] That's our Max!

909
00:28:14,300 --> 00:28:16,133
(laughing)

910
00:28:16,133 --> 00:28:17,367
- [Joel] This is
just like Hooper.

911
00:28:17,367 --> 00:28:19,667
- Yeah, or, uh, Kenny
Rogers in Six Pack.

912
00:28:19,667 --> 00:28:21,000
- [Tom] Or E.T.

913
00:28:21,000 --> 00:28:22,100
Oh, wait.

914
00:28:22,100 --> 00:28:23,667
- Hold on.

915
00:28:23,667 --> 00:28:25,733
- Hey, I'm on the phone
to the coast here.

916
00:28:25,733 --> 00:28:28,667
- Okay, half pepperoni,
half mushroom.

917
00:28:28,667 --> 00:28:29,767
- Go get her.

918
00:28:32,000 --> 00:28:33,167
- [Tom] Hi, you come here often?

919
00:28:33,167 --> 00:28:34,000
Uh, wait.

920
00:28:38,933 --> 00:28:41,633
- [Joel] Oh, it must
have hit a springboard.

921
00:28:41,633 --> 00:28:44,633
- [Tom] Grandpa
Ninja saves the day.

922
00:28:47,000 --> 00:28:50,500
- Oh, what is he, Obi
fricking Wan Kenobi?

923
00:28:53,600 --> 00:28:54,533
- [Carrie] Well,
my brother worked

924
00:28:54,533 --> 00:28:55,767
at the cannery for four years.

925
00:28:55,767 --> 00:28:56,767
- My brother lives in Florida.

926
00:28:56,767 --> 00:28:57,867
- A lot of trouble.

927
00:28:57,867 --> 00:28:59,967
And then he just disappeared.

928
00:28:59,967 --> 00:29:02,433
But see, that's not
in character at all.

929
00:29:02,433 --> 00:29:03,700
- [Tom] Gerbil check.

930
00:29:03,700 --> 00:29:05,567
- Not for someone who
cared enough to raise

931
00:29:05,567 --> 00:29:06,967
me alone all those years.

932
00:29:06,967 --> 00:29:08,700
(snoring)

933
00:29:08,700 --> 00:29:10,200
- My parents were
killed in an accident.

934
00:29:10,200 --> 00:29:11,467
- [Joel] That's nice

935
00:29:11,467 --> 00:29:13,100
- My brother was just
that close to putting

936
00:29:13,100 --> 00:29:14,500
a union in that cannery.

937
00:29:14,500 --> 00:29:16,100
- Then he became the
president of Poland.

938
00:29:16,100 --> 00:29:19,133
- [Carrie] I know that this
must sound real crazy to y'all--

939
00:29:19,133 --> 00:29:20,700
- [Joel] But I eat light bulbs.

940
00:29:20,700 --> 00:29:22,400
- If y'all know what a
hold that Chad Webster

941
00:29:22,400 --> 00:29:23,600
has on this town.

942
00:29:23,600 --> 00:29:25,233
- You're saying Webster
killed your brother?

943
00:29:25,233 --> 00:29:26,667
- [Tom] Emmanuel Lewis
killed her brother?

944
00:29:26,667 --> 00:29:28,867
- Take a left right here.

945
00:29:28,867 --> 00:29:30,200
- Did you go to the police?

946
00:29:30,200 --> 00:29:31,133
- Yeah.

947
00:29:31,133 --> 00:29:32,967
But just, there's just no proof.

948
00:29:32,967 --> 00:29:36,100
- Just a lot of things that
don't add up to anything else.

949
00:29:36,100 --> 00:29:37,700
- [Tom] Oh,
trigonometry, of course.

950
00:29:37,700 --> 00:29:38,867
- Persons report.

951
00:29:38,867 --> 00:29:41,033
- And I filed my nails.

952
00:29:41,033 --> 00:29:42,033
- How many others?

953
00:29:42,033 --> 00:29:43,533
- Four.

954
00:29:43,533 --> 00:29:44,900
They'd all been working
at the cannery for years,

955
00:29:44,900 --> 00:29:47,533
all friends of my brothers,
all troublemakers.

956
00:29:47,533 --> 00:29:48,933
- [Tom] And they're all
here tonight on Tattletales!

957
00:29:48,933 --> 00:29:50,233
(imitating crowd cheering)

958
00:29:50,233 --> 00:29:52,067
- One day, gone.

959
00:29:52,067 --> 00:29:54,000
Greener pastures.

960
00:29:54,000 --> 00:29:55,867
- Uh, what'd you say?

961
00:29:55,867 --> 00:29:57,067
I was thinking about my tongue.

962
00:29:57,067 --> 00:29:58,367
- That they didn't just leave.

963
00:29:58,367 --> 00:29:59,300
- [Joel] You know you're boring

964
00:29:59,300 --> 00:30:00,900
when you're boring a Van Patten.

965
00:30:00,900 --> 00:30:01,733
- Yeah.

966
00:30:01,733 --> 00:30:02,967
(whistling)

967
00:30:02,967 --> 00:30:05,733
- [Tom] Uh, you want
to pop in a tape?

968
00:30:07,200 --> 00:30:08,900
- This is the house
is on the left.

969
00:30:08,900 --> 00:30:11,800
- [Joel] Just keep saying to
yourself, it's only a movie.

970
00:30:11,800 --> 00:30:13,733
Last house on the left.

971
00:30:15,167 --> 00:30:16,533
- Oh, just, uh, just park
in the middle of the street,

972
00:30:16,533 --> 00:30:18,133
and, uh, leave the lights on.

973
00:30:18,133 --> 00:30:19,067
No problem.

974
00:30:20,267 --> 00:30:22,567
- [Tom] We deliver union
organizers overnight.

975
00:30:22,567 --> 00:30:24,067
- [Joel] I'm free!

976
00:30:25,300 --> 00:30:26,733
- [Carrie] Thank you.

977
00:30:26,733 --> 00:30:27,900
- Are you sure there's
nothing we could do to help?

978
00:30:27,900 --> 00:30:29,367
- No, there's
nothing you can do.

979
00:30:29,367 --> 00:30:30,400
But thank you.

980
00:30:30,400 --> 00:30:31,467
Good night.

981
00:30:31,467 --> 00:30:32,700
- [Both] Night.

982
00:30:33,667 --> 00:30:35,667
- Tim, you're an idiot.

983
00:30:35,667 --> 00:30:36,967
- [Max] Now that's
some lady, huh?

984
00:30:36,967 --> 00:30:38,333
- [Tom] No, that's my wife.

985
00:30:38,333 --> 00:30:39,867
- Too bad we can't help her.

986
00:30:39,867 --> 00:30:42,100
- Listen, pal, if you think
I'm walking away from her,

987
00:30:42,100 --> 00:30:44,867
Webster, the cannery,
or this town, you're--

988
00:30:44,867 --> 00:30:46,100
- You're absolutely right.

989
00:30:46,100 --> 00:30:47,600
Let's get out of here.

990
00:30:47,600 --> 00:30:49,000
- [Max] Guess you figured
that out already, huh?

991
00:30:49,000 --> 00:30:50,667
- We've been told
to get out of town.

992
00:30:50,667 --> 00:30:51,533
- By who?

993
00:30:51,533 --> 00:30:52,567
- Try a guess.

994
00:30:52,567 --> 00:30:53,867
- Webster?

995
00:30:53,867 --> 00:30:54,867
- Good guess.

996
00:30:54,867 --> 00:30:56,133
- [Joel] Noah Webster?

997
00:30:56,133 --> 00:30:57,267
- We're not leaving.

998
00:30:57,267 --> 00:30:58,833
Nobody's running me out of town.

999
00:30:58,833 --> 00:31:00,367
- [Tom] Nobody's
running me out of town.

1000
00:31:00,367 --> 00:31:01,700
- We're not leaving.

1001
00:31:01,700 --> 00:31:03,467
Figure something out.

1002
00:31:04,767 --> 00:31:06,567
- That's what I was afraid of.

1003
00:31:06,567 --> 00:31:09,567
(imitating timpani)

1004
00:31:10,567 --> 00:31:12,900
- Good morning, how are you?

1005
00:31:14,333 --> 00:31:15,533
Denise, Carol.

1006
00:31:15,533 --> 00:31:16,467
- [Joel] Thank you
for flying Northwest.

1007
00:31:16,467 --> 00:31:18,700
Enjoy your stay in Fargo.

1008
00:31:18,700 --> 00:31:20,367
- Dan, how's that baby?
- [Tom] Haven't had it yet.

1009
00:31:20,367 --> 00:31:22,100
- Annie, what's going on here?

1010
00:31:22,100 --> 00:31:22,933
Nobody's talking to me.

1011
00:31:22,933 --> 00:31:24,167
- [Tom] Susan Sarandon.

1012
00:31:24,167 --> 00:31:25,333
- Boss says you're
trouble, Carrie.

1013
00:31:25,333 --> 00:31:27,067
No one wants to be
caught speaking to you.

1014
00:31:27,067 --> 00:31:28,667
- [Joel] Oh, are they going
to sing Matchmaker now?

1015
00:31:28,667 --> 00:31:29,767
- [Tom] Looks like it.

1016
00:31:29,767 --> 00:31:31,267
- I'm really sorry.

1017
00:31:31,267 --> 00:31:32,500
- But you're going to the
meeting this afternoon.

1018
00:31:32,500 --> 00:31:33,600
- Oh, you're going
to that meeting.

1019
00:31:33,600 --> 00:31:34,767
- Not with us.

1020
00:31:39,333 --> 00:31:40,167
- [Tom] Hi, Frodo.

1021
00:31:40,167 --> 00:31:41,000
Hi, Axl.

1022
00:31:41,000 --> 00:31:41,933
Hi, Divine.

1023
00:31:45,067 --> 00:31:46,200
- It's really good today.

1024
00:31:46,200 --> 00:31:47,700
- [Joel] M-hm, nummy.

1025
00:31:47,700 --> 00:31:49,300
- What's weird is that
this is a Chrysler plant.

1026
00:31:49,300 --> 00:31:51,300
I don't know what all
this meat is doing.

1027
00:31:51,300 --> 00:31:53,733
- [Joel] Hey, Huey Lewis.

1028
00:31:53,733 --> 00:31:54,700
- [Tom] And a whole pie.

1029
00:31:54,700 --> 00:31:56,567
Uh, uh, want anything?

1030
00:31:56,567 --> 00:32:00,200
- I don't need to tell you
what happened last night, do I?

1031
00:32:00,200 --> 00:32:02,833
Carrie Brown is more
trouble than her brother.

1032
00:32:02,833 --> 00:32:04,933
And I can't afford to
waste any more time on her.

1033
00:32:04,933 --> 00:32:07,633
- [Tom] The lights are
on, but Fatty's not home.

1034
00:32:07,633 --> 00:32:08,633
- I know she's a problem.

1035
00:32:08,633 --> 00:32:09,767
But I think--

1036
00:32:09,767 --> 00:32:10,833
- Don't start
thinking, Bill Carter.

1037
00:32:10,833 --> 00:32:12,433
- I wouldn't worry about that.

1038
00:32:12,433 --> 00:32:14,300
- I'm telling you,
there's something

1039
00:32:14,300 --> 00:32:15,933
weird about this old man
she's been talking to.

1040
00:32:15,933 --> 00:32:16,867
He makes me nervous.

1041
00:32:16,867 --> 00:32:18,767
And the kid is troublemaker.

1042
00:32:18,767 --> 00:32:21,200
But if Carrie
Brown isn't around,

1043
00:32:21,200 --> 00:32:23,267
then there's no trail
for them to follow.

1044
00:32:23,267 --> 00:32:24,500
- [Joel] Is this a limerick?

1045
00:32:24,500 --> 00:32:25,967
- And they just drift
on to the next town.

1046
00:32:25,967 --> 00:32:27,767
- Jake, you can't
start something like--

1047
00:32:27,767 --> 00:32:29,867
- I'm not starting--
- [Tom] Hooker's a good cop!

1048
00:32:29,867 --> 00:32:31,333
- I'm just finishing
what has to be done.

1049
00:32:31,333 --> 00:32:32,733
- [Joel] Give me a kiss.

1050
00:32:32,733 --> 00:32:35,067
- There's nothing for
you to think about.

1051
00:32:35,067 --> 00:32:37,200
- [Tom] Well, uh,
what about lunch?

1052
00:32:37,200 --> 00:32:40,033
You going to hang
around for that pizza?

1053
00:32:40,033 --> 00:32:42,233
- Just make sure you're
available tonight.

1054
00:32:42,233 --> 00:32:43,867
- [Tom] He asked me!

1055
00:32:43,867 --> 00:32:45,700
I'll wear that
strapless Ed Asner.

1056
00:32:45,700 --> 00:32:46,533
- [Joel] He's gonna blow!

1057
00:32:46,533 --> 00:32:48,500
- [Tom] Look out!

1058
00:32:48,500 --> 00:32:50,133
- Grantsburg, Wisconsin.

1059
00:32:50,133 --> 00:32:53,033
Workers chafing under the
spiked heel of capitalism.

1060
00:32:53,033 --> 00:32:54,700
- Carrie, Carrie.

1061
00:32:54,700 --> 00:32:55,700
- [Tom] I had the seafood plate.

1062
00:32:55,700 --> 00:32:56,767
- Spinning your wheels.

1063
00:32:56,767 --> 00:32:57,733
- My wheels.

1064
00:32:57,733 --> 00:32:59,133
Let me spin them.

1065
00:32:59,133 --> 00:33:01,567
There's got to be
some way to help you.

1066
00:33:01,567 --> 00:33:03,600
- Max, these people
won't even talk to me.

1067
00:33:03,600 --> 00:33:05,000
They say I'm trouble.

1068
00:33:05,000 --> 00:33:06,500
- [Joel] Maxi Priest?

1069
00:33:06,500 --> 00:33:07,900
- [Carrie] There's supposed to
be a meeting this afternoon.

1070
00:33:07,900 --> 00:33:09,167
But I'll be sitting alone.

1071
00:33:09,167 --> 00:33:10,267
- Oh yeah?

1072
00:33:10,267 --> 00:33:11,333
What kind of meeting?

1073
00:33:11,333 --> 00:33:12,500
- A union meeting.

1074
00:33:12,500 --> 00:33:13,900
- [Tom] Oh, they
going to have cookies?

1075
00:33:13,900 --> 00:33:15,500
- There won't be any
meeting or any union.

1076
00:33:15,500 --> 00:33:16,867
Get out of my cannery.

1077
00:33:16,867 --> 00:33:18,433
- So you're canning her.

1078
00:33:18,433 --> 00:33:19,333
How ironic.

1079
00:33:20,967 --> 00:33:23,367
- You want to take a
vote on that, Webster?

1080
00:33:23,367 --> 00:33:25,233
- [Joel] Uh, Max,
this is a cannery.

1081
00:33:25,233 --> 00:33:28,733
- You've got a lot of
people working here.

1082
00:33:29,600 --> 00:33:31,233
I'd say they outvote you 100--

1083
00:33:31,233 --> 00:33:33,500
♪ Look for the union label. ♪

1084
00:33:33,500 --> 00:33:34,500
- [Tom] Come on, everybody.

1085
00:33:34,500 --> 00:33:36,233
Come on, Pete Seeger, come on.

1086
00:33:36,233 --> 00:33:37,067
Weavers, join in.

1087
00:33:37,067 --> 00:33:38,900
Come on, Woody.

1088
00:33:38,900 --> 00:33:41,733
- Can't stop people from
meeting and talking.

1089
00:33:41,733 --> 00:33:43,033
- I told you to get out.

1090
00:33:43,033 --> 00:33:44,300
- Throw me out.

1091
00:33:45,500 --> 00:33:47,567
Loud talk doesn't scare anyone.

1092
00:33:47,567 --> 00:33:49,433
- [Tom] Old Black Eyes is back.

1093
00:33:49,433 --> 00:33:51,467
- You should attend.

1094
00:33:51,467 --> 00:33:53,300
It's your future, too.

1095
00:33:55,567 --> 00:33:56,933
- My hero.

1096
00:33:56,933 --> 00:33:58,500
- [Tom] Mine too.

1097
00:33:58,500 --> 00:34:00,467
- Now I know that none of what
I've said this afternoon is--

1098
00:34:00,467 --> 00:34:01,900
- [Joel] Oh, she's
an Alpha Omega.

1099
00:34:01,900 --> 00:34:03,433
We hate them.

1100
00:34:03,433 --> 00:34:04,600
- Goodness, most of y'all have
been working here much longer

1101
00:34:04,600 --> 00:34:05,833
than I have.

1102
00:34:05,833 --> 00:34:07,667
Your mothers and your
fathers worked here.

1103
00:34:07,667 --> 00:34:10,533
- [Tom] Dominus
vobiscum, everyone.

1104
00:34:10,533 --> 00:34:12,800
- But now we have
to make a change.

1105
00:34:12,800 --> 00:34:15,200
To make a life for us.

1106
00:34:15,200 --> 00:34:17,133
For your kids.

1107
00:34:17,133 --> 00:34:19,433
Now I've got a petition
here for the union.

1108
00:34:19,433 --> 00:34:21,967
And I need 40 more signatures.

1109
00:34:21,967 --> 00:34:23,567
So let's see a show of hands.

1110
00:34:23,567 --> 00:34:25,867
- I lost my hand
in a fish chopper.

1111
00:34:25,867 --> 00:34:29,300
(light electronic music)

1112
00:34:34,400 --> 00:34:35,933
- [Tom] Heh heh heh.

1113
00:34:35,933 --> 00:34:38,467
- [Joel] Studs
Terkel, not working.

1114
00:34:38,467 --> 00:34:39,333
- Huh, Carrie?

1115
00:34:39,333 --> 00:34:40,800
- Charlie.

1116
00:34:40,800 --> 00:34:43,600
- [Tom] I have heard the
stories of the Thugee cult.

1117
00:34:43,600 --> 00:34:45,733
- I can't afford to
give up one day's pay.

1118
00:34:45,733 --> 00:34:47,967
Let alone, paycheck.

1119
00:34:47,967 --> 00:34:49,500
None of us can.

1120
00:34:49,500 --> 00:34:51,000
- [Joel] Howard Johnson's right!

1121
00:34:51,000 --> 00:34:53,033
(murmuring)

1122
00:34:53,033 --> 00:34:55,467
- You know where my
family's at, Carrie.

1123
00:34:55,467 --> 00:34:58,200
- At the trailer park
at the edge of town.

1124
00:34:58,200 --> 00:35:00,900
- Till Bill gets
his health back.

1125
00:35:00,900 --> 00:35:02,667
- [Joel] Delta Burke?

1126
00:35:04,100 --> 00:35:07,133
- I tried applying for a
job at your cannery today.

1127
00:35:07,133 --> 00:35:08,567
Couldn't get in.

1128
00:35:08,567 --> 00:35:10,400
- [Tom] I had no
marketable skills.

1129
00:35:10,400 --> 00:35:11,633
- [Max] I'm not
surprised, though.

1130
00:35:11,633 --> 00:35:13,400
Working conditions
there are so great.

1131
00:35:13,400 --> 00:35:14,733
- Anybody umberstand him?

1132
00:35:14,733 --> 00:35:15,667
- How much?

1133
00:35:15,667 --> 00:35:16,900
$300?

1134
00:35:16,900 --> 00:35:17,967
- [Joel] Hey, he's
doing stand-up.

1135
00:35:17,967 --> 00:35:19,500
He's working the crowd.

1136
00:35:19,500 --> 00:35:21,033
- Looking forward to your
children going to college?

1137
00:35:21,033 --> 00:35:22,967
Because it's not going
to be easy on the salary

1138
00:35:22,967 --> 00:35:24,467
you're making.

1139
00:35:24,467 --> 00:35:25,967
But when the cost-of-living
increases come in every year,

1140
00:35:25,967 --> 00:35:28,200
that'll make things
a whole lot easier.

1141
00:35:28,200 --> 00:35:30,100
I don't know why
Carrie's bothering

1142
00:35:30,100 --> 00:35:31,833
to rock the boat for you people.

1143
00:35:31,833 --> 00:35:32,767
You're doing just fine.

1144
00:35:32,767 --> 00:35:34,000
- He's speaking in tongues.

1145
00:35:34,000 --> 00:35:35,767
- You get paid what
they want to give you.

1146
00:35:35,767 --> 00:35:37,633
You work the hours
they tell you.

1147
00:35:37,633 --> 00:35:40,500
You clock in and punch
out right on time.

1148
00:35:40,500 --> 00:35:42,033
Their time!

1149
00:35:42,033 --> 00:35:44,133
- [Tom] Hey, time is truly a
subjective phenomenon, Tim.

1150
00:35:44,133 --> 00:35:45,967
- Carrie's waiting
for a show of hands.

1151
00:35:45,967 --> 00:35:47,467
She isn't going to get one.

1152
00:35:47,467 --> 00:35:49,033
- Should we have a silent vote?

1153
00:35:49,033 --> 00:35:50,600
- Big Brother
isn't watching you.

1154
00:35:50,600 --> 00:35:52,567
He's got you right
in his hip pocket.

1155
00:35:52,567 --> 00:35:54,400
- [Joel] Huh. Well, I don't
have a problem with that.

1156
00:35:54,400 --> 00:35:55,433
- If you ask me,
you're all getting

1157
00:35:55,433 --> 00:35:56,300
exactly what you deserve.

1158
00:35:56,300 --> 00:35:58,133
- [Tom] We didn't ask.

1159
00:35:59,333 --> 00:36:01,533
- [Joel] Now everyone,
take out your hymnal.

1160
00:36:01,533 --> 00:36:04,933
(clapping and whistling)

1161
00:36:08,000 --> 00:36:08,867
- I'll sign.

1162
00:36:08,867 --> 00:36:10,100
- You're fired.

1163
00:36:11,233 --> 00:36:12,167
- [Woman] I'll sign.

1164
00:36:12,167 --> 00:36:12,967
- You're fired, you're fired.

1165
00:36:12,967 --> 00:36:14,600
You're fired, too.

1166
00:36:14,600 --> 00:36:17,433
- [Tom] We feel
confident, secure.

1167
00:36:19,567 --> 00:36:22,833
- [All] Attica,
Attica, Attica, Attica!

1168
00:36:25,000 --> 00:36:26,233
- [Joel] Mmm, Tahitian Treat.

1169
00:36:26,233 --> 00:36:28,400
Hope the meeting
didn't start yet.

1170
00:36:28,400 --> 00:36:29,567
Boy, it's cold.

1171
00:36:29,567 --> 00:36:30,533
(burping)

1172
00:36:30,533 --> 00:36:32,167
Oh, yahtzee.

1173
00:36:32,167 --> 00:36:33,033
Oh, hi.

1174
00:36:33,033 --> 00:36:34,600
What's up, gang?

1175
00:36:34,600 --> 00:36:36,733
- You took the last
Tahitian Treat, old man.

1176
00:36:36,733 --> 00:36:38,033
- [Joel] Jimmy Carl Black.

1177
00:36:38,033 --> 00:36:39,600
- [Tom] No, it's Shawn Phillips.

1178
00:36:39,600 --> 00:36:41,067
And Tim Robbins.

1179
00:36:41,067 --> 00:36:42,900
- Just been to church.

1180
00:36:44,067 --> 00:36:46,600
Your young friend
missed his vocation.

1181
00:36:46,600 --> 00:36:48,500
Should've been an evangelist.

1182
00:36:48,500 --> 00:36:49,900
- [Joel] Too much like acting.

1183
00:36:49,900 --> 00:36:51,267
- He does have a way with words.

1184
00:36:51,267 --> 00:36:52,467
- [Tom] Uh, not in
the right order, but--

1185
00:36:52,467 --> 00:36:53,300
- Or you.

1186
00:36:54,633 --> 00:36:55,800
You're leaving Clearwater.

1187
00:36:55,800 --> 00:36:59,100
- You're very nosy, kitty cat.

1188
00:36:59,100 --> 00:37:01,033
You know what we
do to nosy people?

1189
00:37:01,033 --> 00:37:04,967
- You're not going to
get out of this one, pal.

1190
00:37:06,367 --> 00:37:08,500
(grunting)

1191
00:37:08,500 --> 00:37:11,067
(suspenseful orchestral music)

1192
00:37:11,067 --> 00:37:12,900
- [Joel] Thank you,
crotch-rocketed friend.

1193
00:37:12,900 --> 00:37:16,000
- [Tom] Don't forget
to say (mumbling)

1194
00:37:18,033 --> 00:37:21,200
- Okay, we'll just follow
you to the party, then.

1195
00:37:21,200 --> 00:37:23,233
- How long since you've
been on one of these?

1196
00:37:23,233 --> 00:37:24,100
- Long time.

1197
00:37:24,100 --> 00:37:25,300
Feels good.

1198
00:37:25,300 --> 00:37:26,733
- [Joel] Must be
the new seat covers.

1199
00:37:26,733 --> 00:37:27,667
They hit Mr. Bubble!

1200
00:37:27,667 --> 00:37:28,867
- [Tom] Oh no.

1201
00:37:28,867 --> 00:37:29,800
- I don't know if
you're going to enjoy

1202
00:37:29,800 --> 00:37:32,100
the experience all that much.

1203
00:37:33,633 --> 00:37:36,067
- [Tom] Lean into it.

1204
00:37:36,067 --> 00:37:37,700
- Hold on!

1205
00:37:37,700 --> 00:37:38,800
- [Tom] Sunday, at
Great Lakes Dragaway

1206
00:37:38,800 --> 00:37:40,967
in Union Grove, Wisconsin!

1207
00:37:43,233 --> 00:37:46,167
Mighty Mikes, with
action traction.

1208
00:37:47,467 --> 00:37:48,533
Lean into it.

1209
00:37:49,600 --> 00:37:52,533
(imitating engine)

1210
00:37:53,367 --> 00:37:54,700
- A garden weasel!

1211
00:37:54,700 --> 00:37:55,533
- [Tom] Ooh.

1212
00:37:55,533 --> 00:37:56,400
Where did he have that?

1213
00:37:56,400 --> 00:37:57,867
- [Joel] Hi-Keeba.

1214
00:37:57,867 --> 00:37:58,700
Huzzah.

1215
00:38:02,700 --> 00:38:04,267
- He's off the ramp.

1216
00:38:04,267 --> 00:38:05,200
- [Joel] What ramp?

1217
00:38:05,200 --> 00:38:07,367
- Hair blowing in the wind.

1218
00:38:08,200 --> 00:38:09,600
My colon.

1219
00:38:09,600 --> 00:38:13,500
- [Joel] Oh, I saw that
in a Mapplethorpe film.

1220
00:38:14,700 --> 00:38:18,233
- [Tom] Um, why don't
they just turn right?

1221
00:38:19,467 --> 00:38:21,133
- Oh, I'll harm you.

1222
00:38:29,000 --> 00:38:30,467
- [Tom] Hey.

1223
00:38:30,467 --> 00:38:31,533
Hey, I just wanted to tell
you you got a tail light out.

1224
00:38:31,533 --> 00:38:32,367
Gee.

1225
00:38:34,600 --> 00:38:36,300
- [Joel] He's got
a licorice whip.

1226
00:38:36,300 --> 00:38:38,733
- Yippee-yi-ay, tie-ay, cowboy!

1227
00:38:38,733 --> 00:38:39,567
Tay.

1228
00:38:41,133 --> 00:38:42,767
- Where'd you learn that one?

1229
00:38:42,767 --> 00:38:44,000
- Motorcycle school.

1230
00:38:44,000 --> 00:38:45,667
- [Tom] You're cute.

1231
00:38:50,233 --> 00:38:53,133
(tires screeching)

1232
00:38:55,467 --> 00:38:57,267
- [Joel] That'll happen.

1233
00:38:57,267 --> 00:38:58,367
- [Tom] Yeah.

1234
00:39:00,333 --> 00:39:02,067
- [Max] Where's Carrie?
- [Lee] At a union meeting.

1235
00:39:02,067 --> 00:39:03,600
- [Max] We'd better
get to her tonight.

1236
00:39:03,600 --> 00:39:04,767
- [Tom] It's potluck.

1237
00:39:04,767 --> 00:39:06,933
We've got to bring a dish.

1238
00:39:15,900 --> 00:39:17,400
(whistling)

1239
00:39:17,400 --> 00:39:18,233
- Lee?

1240
00:39:18,233 --> 00:39:19,467
Oh, Lee.

1241
00:39:19,467 --> 00:39:20,367
- [Joel] Lee.

1242
00:39:20,367 --> 00:39:21,600
- Here, boy.

1243
00:39:21,600 --> 00:39:23,733
- [Joel] Oh, couldn't
you stay in the van?

1244
00:39:23,733 --> 00:39:25,067
- We were right.

1245
00:39:26,967 --> 00:39:27,900
Carrie?

1246
00:39:27,900 --> 00:39:28,833
Carrie, it's Max.

1247
00:39:28,833 --> 00:39:31,300
- [Tom] It's a medieval house.

1248
00:39:33,500 --> 00:39:35,033
- [Joel] They
varnished my house.

1249
00:39:35,033 --> 00:39:35,933
- You all right?

1250
00:39:35,933 --> 00:39:37,433
- What's happened?

1251
00:39:37,433 --> 00:39:40,500
- I found it like
this when I came home.

1252
00:39:40,500 --> 00:39:45,500
- They disconnected cable and
hooked up my stereo all wrong.

1253
00:39:46,933 --> 00:39:48,533
- They've torn the place apart.

1254
00:39:48,533 --> 00:39:49,433
- Nice flat.

1255
00:39:49,433 --> 00:39:51,333
Apartment, I mean.

1256
00:39:51,333 --> 00:39:52,300
- It's going to be okay.

1257
00:39:52,300 --> 00:39:54,067
We won't let them get you.

1258
00:39:54,067 --> 00:39:55,300
- [Tom] Hey look,
Ignatz was here.

1259
00:39:55,300 --> 00:39:57,733
- [Joel] Oh, Bil Keane
ransacked the apartment.

1260
00:39:57,733 --> 00:39:59,100
- [Tom] Or Billy did it.

1261
00:39:59,100 --> 00:40:00,200
Billy did it.

1262
00:40:00,200 --> 00:40:01,833
- I know they killed my brother.

1263
00:40:01,833 --> 00:40:04,067
And now they're after me.

1264
00:40:04,067 --> 00:40:05,533
(throat clearing)

1265
00:40:05,533 --> 00:40:09,567
- [Tom] How about a
little sugar for grandpa?

1266
00:40:09,567 --> 00:40:11,000
- Leave it to us.

1267
00:40:16,067 --> 00:40:17,267
(door closing)

1268
00:40:17,267 --> 00:40:19,767
- [Tom] Well, that's,
what do we do now?

1269
00:40:19,767 --> 00:40:20,867
- Big, brave girl.

1270
00:40:20,867 --> 00:40:22,133
- Well, brave, anyway.

1271
00:40:22,133 --> 00:40:24,367
- I stir everything up
and I can't handle it.

1272
00:40:24,367 --> 00:40:25,933
- They've warned you, okay?

1273
00:40:25,933 --> 00:40:27,367
Now it's up to us.

1274
00:40:27,367 --> 00:40:28,933
We're going to nail
Webster for good.

1275
00:40:28,933 --> 00:40:30,300
You just sit tight.

1276
00:40:30,300 --> 00:40:32,167
They won't be back.

1277
00:40:32,167 --> 00:40:33,800
But we will.

1278
00:40:33,800 --> 00:40:35,133
- [Tom] We won't let the seniors

1279
00:40:35,133 --> 00:40:37,633
beat up on you anymore, Honey.

1280
00:40:39,133 --> 00:40:39,933
- Ecch.

1281
00:40:41,100 --> 00:40:43,133
- [Joel] You kiss better
than the union boss.

1282
00:40:43,133 --> 00:40:44,033
- [Tom] Oh!

1283
00:40:46,867 --> 00:40:48,067
Dr. Pepper lip gloss.

1284
00:40:48,067 --> 00:40:48,867
