- What would that be?

1541
00:49:37,033 --> 00:49:38,467
- You get off on it.

1542
00:49:38,467 --> 00:49:39,900
It's a thrill, a kick.

1543
00:49:39,900 --> 00:49:40,733
- Kicks!

1544
00:49:40,733 --> 00:49:42,200
- The power you have.

1545
00:49:42,200 --> 00:49:43,100
Life and death.

1546
00:49:43,100 --> 00:49:44,300
(coughing)

1547
00:49:44,300 --> 00:49:45,933
- It's a tough act to top.

1548
00:49:45,933 --> 00:49:47,167
- What I feel and
what I think isn't

1549
00:49:47,167 --> 00:49:49,367
going to matter to you
much longer, Keller.

1550
00:49:49,367 --> 00:49:50,733
Any more than it does--

1551
00:49:50,733 --> 00:49:51,567
(coughing)

1552
00:49:51,567 --> 00:49:52,767
- Hey, hey!

1553
00:49:52,767 --> 00:49:54,500
More dirt in the hole,
less on my shoes.

1554
00:49:54,500 --> 00:49:55,700
- Or you, Carter,

1555
00:49:55,700 --> 00:49:56,533
(gun cocking)

1556
00:49:56,533 --> 00:49:57,467
- Me?

1557
00:49:57,467 --> 00:49:58,733
- Didn't I tell you, Carter?

1558
00:49:58,733 --> 00:50:00,600
After 35 years of
keeping your nose clean

1559
00:50:00,600 --> 00:50:05,367
and looking the other
way, this is what you get.

1560
00:50:05,367 --> 00:50:06,200
(suspenseful orchestral music)

1561
00:50:06,200 --> 00:50:07,100
- I'm not dead yet.

1562
00:50:07,100 --> 00:50:08,267
- [Tom] Uh oh.

1563
00:50:12,533 --> 00:50:13,600
- [Tom] Dirt man.

1564
00:50:13,600 --> 00:50:14,833
In color.

1565
00:50:14,833 --> 00:50:17,933
- I hope he doesn't
soil his ninja robes.

1566
00:50:17,933 --> 00:50:19,633
(cackling)

1567
00:50:19,633 --> 00:50:21,067
- [Tom] Terrible.

1568
00:50:22,167 --> 00:50:23,100
- Ooh.

1569
00:50:23,100 --> 00:50:24,400
Have you learned the plot?

1570
00:50:24,400 --> 00:50:25,233
(cackling)

1571
00:50:25,233 --> 00:50:26,067
- [Tom] Stop it.

1572
00:50:26,067 --> 00:50:26,900
- [Joel] Stop it.

1573
00:50:26,900 --> 00:50:28,167
I feel so dirty.

1574
00:50:28,167 --> 00:50:31,100
I'll just be by the
tree, looking cute.

1575
00:50:32,333 --> 00:50:33,767
- [Tom] Oof, oof.

1576
00:50:35,600 --> 00:50:38,600
That's the sound
of cardboard boxes.

1577
00:50:39,633 --> 00:50:40,800
Oh no, that's the Rosetta stone.

1578
00:50:40,800 --> 00:50:41,633
Don't, oh.

1579
00:50:41,633 --> 00:50:43,533
- Rock, paper, scissor.

1580
00:50:45,267 --> 00:50:46,067
- Thanks.

1581
00:50:49,367 --> 00:50:51,033
- [Tom] Uh, I was just
reaching for the Snickers bar

1582
00:50:51,033 --> 00:50:52,800
in the glove box, boss.

1583
00:50:52,800 --> 00:50:56,833
- [Joel] Hey, Butterball,
that's for Dom DeLuise.

1584
00:50:59,867 --> 00:51:01,300
He's got trouble in spades.

1585
00:51:01,300 --> 00:51:02,467
- [Tom] Ho ho!

1586
00:51:03,600 --> 00:51:06,767
- Don't forget to have
your ninja spayed.

1587
00:51:07,867 --> 00:51:10,167
- [Tom] Hey, he's Little John.

1588
00:51:10,167 --> 00:51:12,433
(grunting)

1589
00:51:16,367 --> 00:51:18,600
- Well, are you
digging this theme?

1590
00:51:18,600 --> 00:51:19,533
(cackling)

1591
00:51:19,533 --> 00:51:21,367
- [Joel] Stop him, stop him.

1592
00:51:21,367 --> 00:51:22,633
Thank you.

1593
00:51:22,633 --> 00:51:24,067
Ooh, right in the keister.

1594
00:51:24,067 --> 00:51:25,733
- [Tom] Kunta Kinte.

1595
00:51:27,800 --> 00:51:30,100
- Hit him, it's dark.
- [Tom] No one will know.

1596
00:51:30,100 --> 00:51:31,100
Oh, rats.

1597
00:51:31,100 --> 00:51:32,367
- I know.

1598
00:51:32,367 --> 00:51:33,733
Lowered heartbeat
to barely a pulse.

1599
00:51:33,733 --> 00:51:35,033
Close your door to the senses

1600
00:51:35,033 --> 00:51:36,300
like you did in the motel room.

1601
00:51:36,300 --> 00:51:37,867
- [Joel] No, I was
really dead, Tim.

1602
00:51:37,867 --> 00:51:38,833
I'm the Reanimator.

1603
00:51:38,833 --> 00:51:41,233
- On the edge of death.

1604
00:51:41,233 --> 00:51:44,500
It can only be
effective once or twice.

1605
00:51:44,500 --> 00:51:45,767
More than that--

1606
00:51:45,767 --> 00:51:47,400
- [Tom] It loses its impact.

1607
00:51:47,400 --> 00:51:49,100
- Could prove fatal.

1608
00:51:49,100 --> 00:51:49,933
- Do it again.

1609
00:51:49,933 --> 00:51:50,767
I dare you.

1610
00:51:50,767 --> 00:51:51,733
- I'm glad you're alive.

1611
00:51:51,733 --> 00:51:53,367
- I prefer it.

1612
00:51:53,367 --> 00:51:56,100
- [Joel] We are
good friends, Tim.

1613
00:51:56,100 --> 00:51:58,900
(imitating music)

1614
00:52:00,433 --> 00:52:01,233
- [Tom] Epilogue, where you
always get to see Lee's gut.

1615
00:52:01,233 --> 00:52:02,533
Yep, and there it is.

1616
00:52:02,533 --> 00:52:03,467
You see what I mean?

1617
00:52:03,467 --> 00:52:04,300
- [Max] When does it happen.

1618
00:52:04,300 --> 00:52:05,933
- Oh, about in a week.

1619
00:52:05,933 --> 00:52:07,167
But listen.

1620
00:52:07,167 --> 00:52:09,167
I want to thank
y'all for proving

1621
00:52:09,167 --> 00:52:11,833
something that I believed in.

1622
00:52:11,833 --> 00:52:13,133
- [Joel] You cannot act.

1623
00:52:13,133 --> 00:52:14,500
- Sorry about your
brother, Carrie.

1624
00:52:14,500 --> 00:52:16,333
- Well, at least I
know for sure, now.

1625
00:52:16,333 --> 00:52:17,667
I needed to.

1626
00:52:17,667 --> 00:52:18,500
- Sob, sob.

1627
00:52:18,500 --> 00:52:19,367
Remorse, remorse.

1628
00:52:19,367 --> 00:52:20,833
Well!

1629
00:52:20,833 --> 00:52:24,767
- If you still need a job, I
can get you one with the union.

1630
00:52:24,767 --> 00:52:26,600
- I'll be in the van with Henry.

1631
00:52:26,600 --> 00:52:29,267
- [Tom] Reading Of Mice and Men.

1632
00:52:30,467 --> 00:52:31,433
- A classy guy.

1633
00:52:31,433 --> 00:52:32,667
- He's an idiot.

1634
00:52:32,667 --> 00:52:33,900
- I still don't know how
you made those people

1635
00:52:33,900 --> 00:52:35,633
think he was dead.

1636
00:52:35,633 --> 00:52:37,633
- It's a long
story, going back--

1637
00:52:37,633 --> 00:52:39,367
- [Joel] Oh, an hour.

1638
00:52:40,833 --> 00:52:41,967
- Listen, about that job.

1639
00:52:41,967 --> 00:52:42,933
- You're fired.

1640
00:52:42,933 --> 00:52:44,533
- [Tom] Heh heh heh heh.

1641
00:52:44,533 --> 00:52:45,733
- I've got to go, Carrie.

1642
00:52:45,733 --> 00:52:46,567
- No.

1643
00:52:46,567 --> 00:52:48,067
- Oh.

1644
00:52:48,067 --> 00:52:49,600
- There's someone we have
to find for the master.

1645
00:52:49,600 --> 00:52:50,633
- The master?

1646
00:52:51,667 --> 00:52:52,500
- My friend.

1647
00:52:52,500 --> 00:52:54,000
It's kind of a nickname.

1648
00:52:54,000 --> 00:52:56,167
Hey, I'll be back this
way for next year's race.

1649
00:52:56,167 --> 00:52:57,433
- You better be.

1650
00:52:57,433 --> 00:52:58,533
- [Tom] Because I'll
be of legal age then.

1651
00:52:58,533 --> 00:52:59,800
- [Joel] Hey.

1652
00:52:59,800 --> 00:53:01,500
- [Tom] Sorry.

1653
00:53:01,500 --> 00:53:04,500
- [Joel] Oh, she
tastes like salmon.

1654
00:53:05,933 --> 00:53:07,367
What are we in the middle of?

1655
00:53:07,367 --> 00:53:08,200
- [Tom] What's this?

1656
00:53:08,200 --> 00:53:09,333
- Take my hand.

1657
00:53:09,333 --> 00:53:10,767
- [Tom] I'm a
stranger in paradise.

1658
00:53:10,767 --> 00:53:12,867
- [Joel] But there's
nothing wrong with my car!

1659
00:53:12,867 --> 00:53:14,100
- Now!

1660
00:53:14,100 --> 00:53:15,600
Pull up.

1661
00:53:15,600 --> 00:53:17,067
- [Alicia] I can't do it.
- Grab hold of the wire.

1662
00:53:17,067 --> 00:53:20,067
- [Tom] We missed something.

1663
00:53:20,067 --> 00:53:21,300
- [Joel] Who's that?

1664
00:53:21,300 --> 00:53:24,133
(imitating pilot)

1665
00:53:26,767 --> 00:53:31,100
- [Tom] OK, see if you can
shake her loose now, Tim.

1666
00:53:33,200 --> 00:53:34,833
- [Joel] Next week, on Mannix.

1667
00:53:34,833 --> 00:53:37,667
(imitating music)

1668
00:53:39,133 --> 00:53:40,700
- [Tom] Hey look, Bud Cort's
up at the top of the cliff,

1669
00:53:40,700 --> 00:53:41,900
playing a banjo.

1670
00:53:41,900 --> 00:53:43,600
- [Joel] Matt Houston.

1671
00:53:43,600 --> 00:53:44,433
In color.

1672
00:53:48,200 --> 00:53:51,167
♪ Those magnificent men in
their flying machines. ♪

1673
00:53:51,167 --> 00:53:52,033
- All right.

1674
00:53:52,033 --> 00:53:53,733
See that guy down there?

1675
00:53:53,733 --> 00:53:54,967
- Jump on him.

1676
00:53:54,967 --> 00:53:56,400
- I'm going to drop
you off right by him.

1677
00:53:56,400 --> 00:53:57,367
- No, I--

1678
00:53:57,367 --> 00:53:58,367
- [Tom] Ew, ew. I hate him, ew.

1679
00:53:58,367 --> 00:53:59,633
- It's going to be okay.

1680
00:53:59,633 --> 00:54:01,700
When I tell you
to drop, you drop.

1681
00:54:01,700 --> 00:54:04,133
- [Joel] What in the Sam, oh.

1682
00:54:05,333 --> 00:54:07,633
- [Max] Look, going to
drop her right by you.

1683
00:54:07,633 --> 00:54:09,333
So be ready.

1684
00:54:09,333 --> 00:54:11,433
- Timothy Van
Patten is Sky King.

1685
00:54:11,433 --> 00:54:12,933
- [Tom] Brought
to you by Nabisco.

1686
00:54:12,933 --> 00:54:13,933
- Coming in.

1687
00:54:18,900 --> 00:54:20,367
Drop!

1688
00:54:20,367 --> 00:54:22,933
- [Joel] Well, she is kind
of a blonde bombshell.

1689
00:54:22,933 --> 00:54:25,033
- [Tom] It's kind of a stretch.

1690
00:54:25,033 --> 00:54:25,867
Ouch.

1691
00:54:27,867 --> 00:54:30,933
- And in an unrelated incident,
a car pulled over today.

1692
00:54:30,933 --> 00:54:31,833
More later.

1693
00:54:33,700 --> 00:54:35,367
- [Tom] More better.

1694
00:54:36,600 --> 00:54:39,100
- [Joel] Enjoy Red Wing shoes.

1695
00:54:40,467 --> 00:54:41,967
- I like to watch.

1696
00:54:44,300 --> 00:54:45,833
- [Joel] Hey, we lost the sound.

1697
00:54:45,833 --> 00:54:46,900
- No, no, it's--

1698
00:54:46,900 --> 00:54:48,633
- [Joel] Oh, I, Yeah.

1699
00:54:50,700 --> 00:54:52,167
- Hmm.

1700
00:54:52,167 --> 00:54:53,067
- You okay?

1701
00:54:54,067 --> 00:54:55,033
- I'm fine.

1702
00:54:55,033 --> 00:54:55,967
- Yeah.

1703
00:54:55,967 --> 00:54:57,000
- I knew those brakes were gone.

1704
00:54:57,000 --> 00:54:58,333
I should have had them fixed.

1705
00:54:58,333 --> 00:54:59,533
There's just no time.

1706
00:54:59,533 --> 00:55:00,533
I mean, everything's
always too fast.

1707
00:55:00,533 --> 00:55:01,467
My whole life's always been--

1708
00:55:01,467 --> 00:55:02,667
- I should have dropped you.

1709
00:55:02,667 --> 00:55:04,167
- I mean, that last
bend back there,

1710
00:55:04,167 --> 00:55:06,900
I didn't even, I didn't even
think I was going to make it.

1711
00:55:06,900 --> 00:55:07,767
- Slow down.

1712
00:55:07,767 --> 00:55:08,933
Take a breath.

1713
00:55:08,933 --> 00:55:09,600
You're going faster
than the car.

1714
00:55:09,600 --> 00:55:10,433
(laughing)

1715
00:55:10,433 --> 00:55:11,633
- I will.

1716
00:55:11,633 --> 00:55:12,567
I always talk too
fast, especially when

1717
00:55:12,567 --> 00:55:13,900
I'm scared half to death.

1718
00:55:13,900 --> 00:55:14,933
Who are you?

1719
00:55:14,933 --> 00:55:16,600
- Max Keller.

1720
00:55:16,600 --> 00:55:18,033
John McAllister.

1721
00:55:18,033 --> 00:55:20,767
- Oh, I'm Alicia Clayton,
native of California, freckles,

1722
00:55:20,767 --> 00:55:22,733
surfboards, and, uh, fast cars.

1723
00:55:22,733 --> 00:55:24,100
- [Joel] What is
this, The Dating Game?

1724
00:55:24,100 --> 00:55:25,867
(humming)

1725
00:55:25,867 --> 00:55:26,700
- We'll take you home.

1726
00:55:26,700 --> 00:55:28,167
- Uh, wait a minute.

1727
00:55:28,167 --> 00:55:29,667
You saved my life. And
what am I supposed to do?

1728
00:55:29,667 --> 00:55:31,167
What am I supposed
to give you for that?

1729
00:55:31,167 --> 00:55:32,000
- [Joel] Oh, just--

1730
00:55:32,000 --> 00:55:32,867
- A dollar?

1731
00:55:32,867 --> 00:55:33,700
- [Tom] A dollar.

1732
00:55:33,700 --> 00:55:34,533
Good.

1733
00:55:34,533 --> 00:55:35,600
A big dollar.

1734
00:55:37,867 --> 00:55:39,067
- I have an idea.

1735
00:55:39,067 --> 00:55:40,567
- [Tom] Oh, yes.

1736
00:55:40,567 --> 00:55:42,000
- There's a big garden party
this afternoon for family

1737
00:55:42,000 --> 00:55:43,567
and friends of the European
Summit. Will you come?

1738
00:55:43,567 --> 00:55:45,167
- I don't think we'd
be on the guest list.

1739
00:55:45,167 --> 00:55:46,533
- [Joel] Uh, we hate Europe.

1740
00:55:46,533 --> 00:55:47,467
- My father's Senator Clayton.

1741
00:55:47,467 --> 00:55:48,967
He's organizing the party.

1742
00:55:48,967 --> 00:55:50,500
- [Tom] Senator Claghorn?
- Um, uh, do me a favor.

1743
00:55:50,500 --> 00:55:52,533
Don't say anything about
the sports car, okay?

1744
00:55:52,533 --> 00:55:53,867
I mean, he's had to put
up with added security,

1745
00:55:53,867 --> 00:55:55,267
bomb threats, secret
service agents.

1746
00:55:55,267 --> 00:55:56,700
All he needs now
is to hear about

1747
00:55:56,700 --> 00:55:57,533
a reckless-driving daughter.

1748
00:55:57,533 --> 00:55:58,900
Four o'clock.

1749
00:55:58,900 --> 00:55:59,733
Oh, and, uh, black tie.

1750
00:55:59,733 --> 00:56:00,833
Okay?

1751
00:56:00,833 --> 00:56:01,633
- Okay.

1752
00:56:01,633 --> 00:56:02,733
- [Tom] Okay.

1753
00:56:04,500 --> 00:56:05,333
Get in.

1754
00:56:06,300 --> 00:56:07,667
- Well, bye.

1755
00:56:07,667 --> 00:56:09,400
- [Tom] D'oh.

1756
00:56:09,400 --> 00:56:11,500
- [Joel] Hey, shoot some
of this action my way.

1757
00:56:11,500 --> 00:56:13,367
- Maybe I should
have kissed her.

1758
00:56:13,367 --> 00:56:14,733
- Would have been a good move.

1759
00:56:14,733 --> 00:56:16,000
- Garden party?

1760
00:56:17,833 --> 00:56:19,333
- We'll take it.

1761
00:56:19,333 --> 00:56:20,567
- Right.

1762
00:56:20,567 --> 00:56:21,367
- Do you think Rick
Nelson will be there?

1763
00:56:21,367 --> 00:56:22,033
- [Joel] It's possible.

1764
00:56:22,033 --> 00:56:22,867
- [Tom] Maybe.

1765
00:56:22,867 --> 00:56:23,800
Reminiscing.

1766
00:56:23,800 --> 00:56:26,033
Eastern thugs go with flow.

1767
00:56:29,467 --> 00:56:30,467
- Ah, what a cliche.

1768
00:56:30,467 --> 00:56:32,600
A Japanese guy in a GM car.

1769
00:56:32,600 --> 00:56:35,300
- [Tom] Xanadu, stately
home of Charles Foster Kane.

1770
00:56:35,300 --> 00:56:36,133
Cost?

1771
00:56:36,133 --> 00:56:37,600
No one can say.

1772
00:56:37,600 --> 00:56:41,600
(suspenseful orchestral music)

1773
00:56:41,600 --> 00:56:43,433
- [Joel] Looks like
a Paul Klee painting.

1774
00:56:43,433 --> 00:56:44,933
- [Tom] Yeah.

1775
00:56:44,933 --> 00:56:45,967
- [Castile] We'll come from
the west, out of the sun.

1776
00:56:45,967 --> 00:56:48,000
- [Tom] He's got a crown on.

1777
00:56:48,000 --> 00:56:49,500
- [Castile] Here.

1778
00:56:49,500 --> 00:56:51,200
- Senator Clayton won't know
what hit him. We'll be ready.

1779
00:56:51,200 --> 00:56:54,300
Every man knows what
he's supposed to do.

1780
00:56:54,300 --> 00:56:55,667
How many people do
you want killed?

1781
00:56:55,667 --> 00:56:56,767
- How many you up for?

1782
00:56:56,767 --> 00:56:58,033
- No one.

1783
00:56:58,033 --> 00:57:00,233
We'll take what we
came for and out.

1784
00:57:00,233 --> 00:57:03,067
- [Joel] Oh, the military's
wearing Zubaz now.

1785
00:57:03,067 --> 00:57:03,900
- [Tom] Mm, neat.

1786
00:57:03,900 --> 00:57:05,433
I like.

1787
00:57:05,433 --> 00:57:07,467
- Not Sybil Danning, but
an incredible simulation.

1788
00:57:07,467 --> 00:57:08,867
- [Tom] I'll say.

1789
00:57:10,300 --> 00:57:13,567
- Your loyalties must
be with the sect.

1790
00:57:14,700 --> 00:57:15,933
- [Tom] Say Uncle.

1791
00:57:15,933 --> 00:57:17,167
- [Joel] David McCallum.

1792
00:57:17,167 --> 00:57:18,567
- My loyalties are to myself.

1793
00:57:18,567 --> 00:57:19,567
You know that.

1794
00:57:19,567 --> 00:57:20,833
- I can remember--

1795
00:57:20,833 --> 00:57:21,667
(grunting)

1796
00:57:21,667 --> 00:57:22,900
- Don't remember.

1797
00:57:22,900 --> 00:57:25,500
Memories are dangerous
in the wrong hands.

1798
00:57:25,500 --> 00:57:27,167
- [Tom] Remember when you
used to get good work, Dave?

1799
00:57:27,167 --> 00:57:28,100
- Castile.

1800
00:57:28,100 --> 00:57:28,933
- Serena.

1801
00:57:30,933 --> 00:57:33,933
You want liberation for
your people, to free them,

1802
00:57:33,933 --> 00:57:36,967
What makes you think
this is the right way?

1803
00:57:36,967 --> 00:57:38,233
- Liberate this, David.

1804
00:57:38,233 --> 00:57:39,667
- If they don't heed
us, we'll kill them.

1805
00:57:39,667 --> 00:57:41,833
- Yeah, yeah, you'll kill
anyone who standing in your way,

1806
00:57:41,833 --> 00:57:43,800
for the cause.

1807
00:57:43,800 --> 00:57:46,233
That's the burden you carry.

1808
00:57:46,233 --> 00:57:48,400
I stopped believing in causes.

1809
00:57:48,400 --> 00:57:49,967
- [Joel] Now I just
believe in effects.

1810
00:57:49,967 --> 00:57:53,133
- For which we pay you
a great deal of money.

1811
00:57:53,133 --> 00:57:55,700
- Plus Dental and a 401k.

1812
00:57:55,700 --> 00:57:57,867
- I'll get you what you need.

1813
00:57:57,867 --> 00:57:58,733
- [Joel] Peroxide.

1814
00:57:58,733 --> 00:58:00,300
Lots of it.

1815
00:58:00,300 --> 00:58:03,867
- It might even work, If you
do exactly as you're told.

1816
00:58:03,867 --> 00:58:05,467
- She's Skeletor's sister.

1817
00:58:05,467 --> 00:58:06,367
Shelly-tor.

1818
00:58:07,567 --> 00:58:09,767
- What memories will
hold you back then?

1819
00:58:09,767 --> 00:58:11,267
- [Tom] Well, we could
sell their plasma, maybe.

1820
00:58:11,267 --> 00:58:14,367
- Won't cooperate,
you can kill them.

1821
00:58:15,700 --> 00:58:16,967
(dramatic orchestral music)

1822
00:58:16,967 --> 00:58:17,833
- [Joel] Get Noel
Harrison to do it.

1823
00:58:17,833 --> 00:58:18,733
- [Tom] Ba-boom.

1824
00:58:18,733 --> 00:58:19,900
- [Joel] Yeah.

1825
00:58:22,367 --> 00:58:23,800
- [Max] It was a pretty
sheik garden party.

1826
00:58:23,800 --> 00:58:25,067
And I figured the worst
that could happen to us

1827
00:58:25,067 --> 00:58:26,467
was eating a bad hors
d'oeuvres or drinking

1828
00:58:26,467 --> 00:58:28,267
too much champagne, right?

1829
00:58:28,267 --> 00:58:29,733
- [Joel] Right.

1830
00:58:29,733 --> 00:58:30,967
- [Max] Not when
you're with the master.

1831
00:58:30,967 --> 00:58:32,400
- So, more horse dee ovaries?

1832
00:58:32,400 --> 00:58:34,000
There you go.

1833
00:58:34,000 --> 00:58:35,533
- [Tom] David Eisenhower.

1834
00:58:35,533 --> 00:58:36,367
- Hi there.

1835
00:58:36,367 --> 00:58:37,200
Hi.

1836
00:58:37,200 --> 00:58:38,033
How's it going.

1837
00:58:38,033 --> 00:58:38,867
Hi.

1838
00:58:38,867 --> 00:58:39,700
- Hello, there.

1839
00:58:39,700 --> 00:58:40,533
- Hello.

1840
00:58:42,667 --> 00:58:45,267
- [Joel] Who's winning
the Dodger game?

1841
00:58:45,267 --> 00:58:46,100
Oh.

1842
00:58:48,467 --> 00:58:50,100
- Hi, Amy.
- Alicia, I need to ask you--

1843
00:58:50,100 --> 00:58:51,567
- Let me talk to you
in a little bit, okay?

1844
00:58:51,567 --> 00:58:53,000
- [Tom] Kinda looks like
Stevie Nicks in that outfit.

1845
00:58:53,000 --> 00:58:54,500
- [Joel] Yeah, I wouldn't
have recognized her

1846
00:58:54,500 --> 00:58:57,200
