2053
01:05:41,767 --> 01:05:43,000
All I could do was--

2054
01:05:43,000 --> 01:05:44,233
- I can't believe
they actually think

2055
01:05:44,233 --> 01:05:45,467
we had something to
do with that raid.

2056
01:05:45,467 --> 01:05:47,400
- [Tom] I can't believe
I ate the whole thing.

2057
01:05:47,400 --> 01:05:48,433
- Go with him.

2058
01:05:48,433 --> 01:05:49,900
- Edward James Olmos.

2059
01:05:49,900 --> 01:05:51,633
Almost.

2060
01:05:51,633 --> 01:05:52,567
- [Tom] Your father,
your brother Vince,
and your aunt Joyce

2061
01:05:52,567 --> 01:05:53,800
are here to bail you out.

2062
01:05:53,800 --> 01:05:55,133
Get out of here.

2063
01:05:58,000 --> 01:05:58,900
- McCloud.

2064
01:05:58,900 --> 01:06:00,400
- All right, McAllister.

2065
01:06:00,400 --> 01:06:01,267
- [Tom] Alastair?

2066
01:06:01,267 --> 01:06:02,800
- I want some answers.

2067
01:06:02,800 --> 01:06:03,733
- Mine?

2068
01:06:03,733 --> 01:06:05,400
Or the ones you want to hear?

2069
01:06:05,400 --> 01:06:06,867
- [Joel] I can't believe
you're still doing

2070
01:06:06,867 --> 01:06:09,067
that in your act.

2071
01:06:09,067 --> 01:06:10,867
- [Tom] And here's your watch.

2072
01:06:10,867 --> 01:06:12,367
(tires screeching)

2073
01:06:12,367 --> 01:06:16,600
(imitating tires screeching)

2074
01:06:16,600 --> 01:06:17,700
Nice hot rod.

2075
01:06:18,600 --> 01:06:20,100
- Michael, this is KITT.

2076
01:06:20,100 --> 01:06:23,800
I need to be on the set
of St. Elsewhere by four.

2077
01:06:27,933 --> 01:06:30,067
(cheering)

2078
01:06:30,067 --> 01:06:31,367
- I wanna know how
they got through,

2079
01:06:31,367 --> 01:06:32,833
and I want to know quick.

2080
01:06:32,833 --> 01:06:33,933
- [Joel] Is it okay that
we're dressed all the same?

2081
01:06:33,933 --> 01:06:35,133
- They saw a person driving--

2082
01:06:35,133 --> 01:06:36,367
- You can write
that in your report.

2083
01:06:36,367 --> 01:06:37,733
How many hostages were taken?

2084
01:06:37,733 --> 01:06:39,233
- 10.

2085
01:06:39,233 --> 01:06:40,267
All the wives and relatives
of the European delegates.

2086
01:06:40,267 --> 01:06:41,600
And Senator Clayton's--

2087
01:06:41,600 --> 01:06:42,500
- [Joel] Ahh.

2088
01:06:42,500 --> 01:06:44,000
- Bob, where were you?

2089
01:06:44,000 --> 01:06:45,500
- What do you mean, where was
I? Look, we were surprised.

2090
01:06:45,500 --> 01:06:47,000
Now we tried the best we could.

2091
01:06:47,000 --> 01:06:49,033
All my men tried. None of us
could get a clean shot at him.

2092
01:06:49,033 --> 01:06:50,500
- Did we overdress
for this briefing?

2093
01:06:50,500 --> 01:06:51,567
- Any word from the kidnappers?

2094
01:06:51,567 --> 01:06:52,567
- There's nothing yet, Senator.

2095
01:06:52,567 --> 01:06:53,833
- You've blanketed the area?

2096
01:06:53,833 --> 01:06:55,267
- In about four minutes.

2097
01:06:55,267 --> 01:06:56,500
Bob.

2098
01:06:56,500 --> 01:06:58,000
- [Joel] I didn't want
Ted Turner to hear this,

2099
01:06:58,000 --> 01:06:59,833
but he wants to colorize
The Second Hundred Years,

2100
01:06:59,833 --> 01:07:01,400
What do you think?

2101
01:07:01,400 --> 01:07:02,567
- [Tom] You know, in a couple
of years, this whole thing's

2102
01:07:02,567 --> 01:07:03,500
going to be replaced
by a desktop.

2103
01:07:03,500 --> 01:07:04,567
- I don't think it was Carlos.

2104
01:07:04,567 --> 01:07:05,500
And it's not Keljin.

2105
01:07:05,500 --> 01:07:06,500
- [Tom] But it started with a K.

2106
01:07:06,500 --> 01:07:07,433
- In and out.

2107
01:07:07,433 --> 01:07:08,367
Varied personnel.

2108
01:07:08,367 --> 01:07:09,500
- [Tom] Know what I mean?

2109
01:07:09,500 --> 01:07:11,267
- And nobody killed.

2110
01:07:11,267 --> 01:07:12,267
Now who does that sound like?

2111
01:07:12,267 --> 01:07:13,267
- [Tom] Gordon Liddy?

2112
01:07:13,267 --> 01:07:14,100
- A professional.

2113
01:07:14,100 --> 01:07:15,067
- Specifically.

2114
01:07:15,067 --> 01:07:15,933
- Castile?

2115
01:07:15,933 --> 01:07:16,867
- Yup.

2116
01:07:16,867 --> 01:07:19,267
He entered Miami two days ago.

2117
01:07:19,267 --> 01:07:20,467
We lost him in the Rockies.

2118
01:07:20,467 --> 01:07:21,733
- How dangerous is he?

2119
01:07:21,733 --> 01:07:22,967
- Oh, I'd put him
in the top three.

2120
01:07:22,967 --> 01:07:24,033
- What are you
guys talking about?

2121
01:07:24,033 --> 01:07:24,900
- [Tom] No clue.

2122
01:07:24,900 --> 01:07:26,133
- Gee.

2123
01:07:26,133 --> 01:07:27,333
- He's long since
given up caring.

2124
01:07:27,333 --> 01:07:28,767
- Well, what do
you think he wants?

2125
01:07:28,767 --> 01:07:30,633
- It's not what he wants.
It's what they want.

2126
01:07:30,633 --> 01:07:31,767
- [Tom] It's like
a tennis match.

2127
01:07:31,767 --> 01:07:32,700
- Who?

2128
01:07:32,700 --> 01:07:33,500
- [Joel] That's what I'm asking.

2129
01:07:33,500 --> 01:07:34,700
- [All] Third base!

2130
01:07:34,700 --> 01:07:36,100
- But he has had a
particular association

2131
01:07:36,100 --> 01:07:37,833
with one group of
terrorists over the years.

2132
01:07:37,833 --> 01:07:39,867
They call themselves
Freedom Fighters.

2133
01:07:39,867 --> 01:07:41,933
- [Tom] Hm, contras?
- Led by a girl named Serena.

2134
01:07:41,933 --> 01:07:42,967
- [Joel] Oh, it's
the Groovie Goolies.

2135
01:07:42,967 --> 01:07:44,200
- That was a long time ago.

2136
01:07:44,200 --> 01:07:45,667
- Ah, with Castile.

2137
01:07:45,667 --> 01:07:46,600
- [Tom] Love his soap.

2138
01:07:46,600 --> 01:07:48,167
- Old loyalties die hard.

2139
01:07:48,167 --> 01:07:49,667
- You know Castile.

2140
01:07:49,667 --> 01:07:50,933
- Oh yeah, I know him.

2141
01:07:50,933 --> 01:07:52,467
- [Tom] Oh, I love their soap.

2142
01:07:52,467 --> 01:07:53,867
- I've tried to
nail him for years.

2143
01:07:53,867 --> 01:07:54,767
- [Tom] Say!

2144
01:07:54,767 --> 01:07:56,233
So has Mallory.

2145
01:07:56,233 --> 01:07:57,867
They've crossed each other's
paths a number of times.

2146
01:07:57,867 --> 01:07:59,800
- Yes, and both of
them still alive.

2147
01:07:59,800 --> 01:08:00,800
- So far.

2148
01:08:00,800 --> 01:08:02,533
Mallory was at the garden party.

2149
01:08:02,533 --> 01:08:03,533
- [Joel] Everyone was there.

2150
01:08:03,533 --> 01:08:04,467
Yoko brought a walrus.

2151
01:08:04,467 --> 01:08:06,133
There was magic in the air.

2152
01:08:06,133 --> 01:08:07,833
- So where the hell is he now?

2153
01:08:07,833 --> 01:08:09,933
- [Tom] He's driving
around in his fabulous

2154
01:08:09,933 --> 01:08:11,333
new Aston Martin!

2155
01:08:11,333 --> 01:08:12,600
(beeping)

2156
01:08:12,600 --> 01:08:16,400
- Could these have come
from ancient astronauts?

2157
01:08:20,667 --> 01:08:22,267
- [Tom] Shut up.

2158
01:08:22,267 --> 01:08:23,533
- Phew, well.

2159
01:08:23,533 --> 01:08:25,200
Even a secret agent has
to go wring out a sock.

2160
01:08:25,200 --> 01:08:26,633
- Shaken, not stirred.

2161
01:08:26,633 --> 01:08:28,567
(laughing)

2162
01:08:28,567 --> 01:08:29,767
- [Tom] For lease?

2163
01:08:29,767 --> 01:08:32,567
Oh boy, I've got
to call my realtor.

2164
01:08:34,267 --> 01:08:37,600
- Oh, he must be president
of the Audobon Society.

2165
01:08:37,600 --> 01:08:38,767
And look, oh.

2166
01:08:38,767 --> 01:08:41,700
- [Joel] He's driving
on the Autobahn.

2167
01:08:42,900 --> 01:08:45,667
- [Tom] Careful,
those are sharp.

2168
01:08:47,133 --> 01:08:48,067
- Ah!

2169
01:08:48,067 --> 01:08:50,067
My ankle bendy-wendy ooh.

2170
01:08:53,400 --> 01:08:55,667
- [Tom] Xanadu, stately
home of, oh, forget it.

2171
01:08:55,667 --> 01:08:59,767
(suspenseful orchestral music)

2172
01:08:59,767 --> 01:09:02,233
- We'd like to thank you for
coming to today's open house.

2173
01:09:02,233 --> 01:09:04,300
You'll be dying here.

2174
01:09:04,300 --> 01:09:06,333
- [Tom] This is the dying room.

2175
01:09:06,333 --> 01:09:09,800
- [Joel] Uh, this'll
be your room.

2176
01:09:09,800 --> 01:09:10,767
- Fits right in.

2177
01:09:10,767 --> 01:09:12,167
- Okay, let's go.

2178
01:09:13,467 --> 01:09:14,800
- Are you okay?

2179
01:09:14,800 --> 01:09:16,333
- Yes.

2180
01:09:16,333 --> 01:09:17,333
- Bars.

2181
01:09:17,333 --> 01:09:18,267
- [Tom] And punch.

2182
01:09:18,267 --> 01:09:19,200
That's what I'm hungry for.

2183
01:09:19,200 --> 01:09:20,967
- We're too high, anyway.

2184
01:09:20,967 --> 01:09:22,100
- [Joel] I know.

2185
01:09:22,100 --> 01:09:23,900
- [Man] There's another
way out of here?

2186
01:09:23,900 --> 01:09:25,233
- Wait a minute.

2187
01:09:26,467 --> 01:09:28,000
(camera shutter clicking)

2188
01:09:28,000 --> 01:09:31,067
- [Tom] It's Brian
Ferry, taking pictures.

2189
01:09:31,067 --> 01:09:32,033
- Yes, yes.

2190
01:09:32,033 --> 01:09:33,233
Work with me.

2191
01:09:33,233 --> 01:09:34,200
Come on, throw
your gutters back.

2192
01:09:34,200 --> 01:09:35,767
Wet your roof, yes.

2193
01:09:39,233 --> 01:09:40,433
She's reading
Little Drummer Girl.

2194
01:09:40,433 --> 01:09:42,067
- [Tom] Oh.

2195
01:09:42,067 --> 01:09:42,900
- Look.

2196
01:09:42,900 --> 01:09:43,733
- [Tom] Where?

2197
01:09:43,733 --> 01:09:44,567
Oh.

2198
01:09:45,967 --> 01:09:47,433
- [Joel] Oh, I've
seen this show.

2199
01:09:47,433 --> 01:09:49,867
It's The Master with the
James Bond no one remembers.

2200
01:09:49,867 --> 01:09:51,600
- [Serena] You know this man.

2201
01:09:51,600 --> 01:09:53,033
- [Castile] Yeah, I know him.

2202
01:09:53,033 --> 01:09:54,933
- [Tom] Brian Ferry.
- Do you want him killed?

2203
01:09:54,933 --> 01:09:56,167
- [Joel] Natch!

2204
01:09:58,600 --> 01:10:00,367
- If it becomes necessary.

2205
01:10:00,367 --> 01:10:02,100
Time to make contact.

2206
01:10:05,667 --> 01:10:06,900
- Thanks.

2207
01:10:06,900 --> 01:10:08,067
Uh, you'll these back
at the end of your trip.

2208
01:10:08,067 --> 01:10:08,900
Thank you.

2209
01:10:08,900 --> 01:10:09,733
(phone ringing)

2210
01:10:09,733 --> 01:10:11,267
- Forbes here.

2211
01:10:11,267 --> 01:10:12,233
- [Joel] Microsoft Service.
Could you hold for an hour?

2212
01:10:12,233 --> 01:10:13,067
- Right, thank you.

2213
01:10:13,067 --> 01:10:14,300
- [Joel] Wait, wait.

2214
01:10:14,300 --> 01:10:15,100
- Control.

2215
01:10:18,233 --> 01:10:19,167
- What do they want?

2216
01:10:19,167 --> 01:10:20,400
- Political prisoners released.

2217
01:10:20,400 --> 01:10:21,733
Jails in Lebanon, France.

2218
01:10:21,733 --> 01:10:22,900
Irish terrorists in England.

2219
01:10:22,900 --> 01:10:24,200
Subversive elements in Berlin.

2220
01:10:24,200 --> 01:10:25,400
About 200--
- And a bucket of chicken.

2221
01:10:25,400 --> 01:10:26,967
- Castile.

2222
01:10:26,967 --> 01:10:28,800
- All right, Castile.

2223
01:10:28,800 --> 01:10:30,000
We've opened negotiations.

2224
01:10:30,000 --> 01:10:31,167
But you have to understand--

2225
01:10:31,167 --> 01:10:32,833
- No, you understand.

2226
01:10:32,833 --> 01:10:34,067
- [Joel] Oh.

2227
01:10:34,067 --> 01:10:35,300
- Finalize negotiations
by six in the morning,

2228
01:10:35,300 --> 01:10:36,733
or we execute the hostages.

2229
01:10:36,733 --> 01:10:38,100
- Now you do that, Castile.

2230
01:10:38,100 --> 01:10:39,367
And you're marked for life.

2231
01:10:39,367 --> 01:10:40,600
There'll be nowhere in
the world you can hide.

2232
01:10:40,600 --> 01:10:42,233
- You can always
hide in the shadows.

2233
01:10:42,233 --> 01:10:43,367
- [Joel] Ooh, he got me on that.

2234
01:10:43,367 --> 01:10:44,867
- You walked right into it.

2235
01:10:44,867 --> 01:10:48,100
- I will contact you
at precisely 0550.

2236
01:10:49,867 --> 01:10:51,500
- [Tom] That's it, huh?

2237
01:10:51,500 --> 01:10:52,767
- Forbes, continue negotiations
with the governments.

2238
01:10:52,767 --> 01:10:53,667
Let them think we're
going through with it.

2239
01:10:53,667 --> 01:10:55,467
- [Joel] Again?

2240
01:10:55,467 --> 01:10:56,533
- What is our plan?

2241
01:10:56,533 --> 01:10:57,933
- Oh, shut up, Mr. Bond.

2242
01:10:57,933 --> 01:10:59,500
- Helicopter assault at dawn.

2243
01:10:59,500 --> 01:11:00,567
- That's crazy.

2244
01:11:00,567 --> 01:11:01,500
You know Castile.

2245
01:11:01,500 --> 01:11:02,367
He's killed hostages before.

2246
01:11:02,367 --> 01:11:03,600
Stockholm, Frankfort.

2247
01:11:03,600 --> 01:11:05,267
- We don't bargain
with terrorists.

2248
01:11:05,267 --> 01:11:06,967
Munich, '72, taught us that.

2249
01:11:06,967 --> 01:11:08,467
- [Tom] Uh, we had numbers then.

2250
01:11:08,467 --> 01:11:09,300
That was at the Olympics.

2251
01:11:09,300 --> 01:11:10,400
- Everyone'll be dead.

2252
01:11:10,400 --> 01:11:11,400
- [Tom] Let's roll.

2253
01:11:11,400 --> 01:11:13,700
- [Joel] We should get going.

2254
01:11:13,700 --> 01:11:15,067
- Hey, photo insert.

2255
01:11:15,067 --> 01:11:16,333
- [Joel] Yeah.

2256
01:11:16,333 --> 01:11:17,567
- One or two men over
that wall and inside,

2257
01:11:17,567 --> 01:11:18,500
before we hit them.

2258
01:11:18,500 --> 01:11:19,800
- That's a sheer, 70-foot wall.

2259
01:11:19,800 --> 01:11:21,333
No human being could climb that.

2260
01:11:21,333 --> 01:11:22,167
- True.

2261
01:11:22,167 --> 01:11:24,067
Unless he were a ninja.

2262
01:11:30,933 --> 01:11:32,167
- No, no, no, no no.

2263
01:11:32,167 --> 01:11:33,800
It's all wrong, Timothy
Van Patten is not

2264
01:11:33,800 --> 01:11:34,833
the type for a gerbil.

2265
01:11:34,833 --> 01:11:35,733
- It's a hamster.

2266
01:11:35,733 --> 01:11:36,967
- Well, whatever.

2267
01:11:36,967 --> 01:11:38,333
He shouldn't be going
around with a Cricetid,

2268
01:11:38,333 --> 01:11:40,400
or any small Slavic
origin rodent.

2269
01:11:40,400 --> 01:11:41,667
It doesn't fit the profile.

2270
01:11:41,667 --> 01:11:42,867
- Ah, you're loony.

2271
01:11:42,867 --> 01:11:44,267
- Well, for your
information, Boris,

2272
01:11:44,267 --> 01:11:45,767
there are plenty
of perfect examples

2273
01:11:45,767 --> 01:11:47,300
of detectives, and other
crime fighting types,

2274
01:11:47,300 --> 01:11:48,933
whose pets were
perfectly suited to them.

2275
01:11:48,933 --> 01:11:50,033
Baretta's cockatoo.

2276
01:11:50,033 --> 01:11:51,733
Sonny Crockett had a crocodile.

2277
01:11:51,733 --> 01:11:53,167
Columbo's basset hound.

2278
01:11:53,167 --> 01:11:54,100
BJ had The Bear.

2279
01:11:54,100 --> 01:11:55,300
- Turner had Hooch.

2280
01:11:55,300 --> 01:11:56,133
- Right, good.

2281
01:11:56,133 --> 01:11:57,033
McCloud had his horse.

2282
01:11:57,033 --> 01:11:57,867
They all make sense.

2283
01:11:57,867 --> 01:11:59,133
- Oh, come on.

2284
01:11:59,133 --> 01:11:59,767
Who went and made
you the expert?

2285
01:11:59,767 --> 01:12:00,767
- Well--

2286
01:12:00,767 --> 01:12:02,000
- Uh, well, actually, I did.

2287
01:12:02,000 --> 01:12:03,400
I wrote a subroutine
into his database,

2288
01:12:03,400 --> 01:12:06,400
allowing him to pair fictional
detectives with pets.

2289
01:12:06,400 --> 01:12:08,300
- Oh, gee, what a useful
bit of programming.

2290
01:12:08,300 --> 01:12:09,233
- Hey.

2291
01:12:09,233 --> 01:12:10,433
- Well, it's something to do.

2292
01:12:10,433 --> 01:12:11,733
I mean, uh, why
don't you, uh, do it

2293
01:12:11,733 --> 01:12:13,867
for us with today's
mumbling hero, you know?

2294
01:12:13,867 --> 01:12:15,700
- Well, I'd suggest a
mandrill for Timothy.

2295
01:12:15,700 --> 01:12:16,700
- A mandrill?

2296
01:12:16,700 --> 01:12:18,300
- What about Magnum, PI?

2297
01:12:18,300 --> 01:12:19,133
- Oh, let's see.

2298
01:12:19,133 --> 01:12:19,967
Something tropical.

2299
01:12:19,967 --> 01:12:20,900
A sea turtle.

2300
01:12:20,900 --> 01:12:21,700
- How about Jim Rockford?

2301
01:12:21,700 --> 01:12:22,467
- Praying mantis.

2302
01:12:22,467 --> 01:12:23,967
- TJ Hooker?

2303
01:12:23,967 --> 01:12:25,200
- Oh, he'd have a creature
with the head of Adrian Zmed

2304
01:12:25,200 --> 01:12:26,400
and the body of a spider monkey.

2305
01:12:26,400 --> 01:12:27,233
- Uh, the Avengers!

2306
01:12:27,233 --> 01:12:28,733
- For Emma Peel, a newt.

2307
01:12:28,733 --> 01:12:30,800
For John Steed, let's see,
a spitting cobra or a duck.

2308
01:12:30,800 --> 01:12:31,733
- Toma?

2309
01:12:31,733 --> 01:12:32,467
- Cockatoo, same as Baretta.

2310
01:12:32,467 --> 01:12:33,300
Next?

2311
01:12:33,300 --> 01:12:34,267
- Uh, Bat Masterson.

2312
01:12:34,267 --> 01:12:35,433
- Penguin.

2313
01:12:35,433 --> 01:12:36,567
All of your 19th century
Western detectives

2314
01:12:36,567 --> 01:12:37,967
would have penguins.

2315
01:12:37,967 --> 01:12:39,233
But there may be a
couple puffins thrown in.

2316
01:12:39,233 --> 01:12:40,100
So be sure to ask
me about each one.

2317
01:12:40,100 --> 01:12:41,367
- Okay.

2318
01:12:41,367 --> 01:12:42,300
- What about, uh,
Starsky and Hutch

2319
01:12:42,300 --> 01:12:43,133
- Paul Michael Glaser, a vicuna.

2320
01:12:43,133 --> 01:12:44,633
David Soul, a bat.

2321
01:12:44,633 --> 01:12:45,833
- Uh, Matlock.

2322
01:12:45,833 --> 01:12:47,133
- He raises mealworms for money.

2323
01:12:47,133 --> 01:12:47,967
- The Saint.

2324
01:12:47,967 --> 01:12:48,800
- Sea cow.

2325
01:12:48,800 --> 01:12:49,633
- Miss Marple.

2326
01:12:49,633 --> 01:12:50,467
- Weasel.

2327
01:12:50,467 --> 01:12:51,333
- Mod Squad?

2328
01:12:51,333 --> 01:12:52,400
- Puppy, lizard, bird.

2329
01:12:52,400 --> 01:12:53,600
- Uh, Charles Darwin.

2330
01:12:53,600 --> 01:12:54,533
- Oh, now, he
wasn't a detective.

2331
01:12:54,533 --> 01:12:55,700
- Well, so?

2332
01:12:55,700 --> 01:12:57,233
He tracked stuff
down, didn't he?

2333
01:12:57,233 --> 01:12:58,767
- It's okay Joel, it's okay.

2334
01:12:58,767 --> 01:13:01,500
Crow, Profesor Darwin
would have a howler monkey

2335
01:13:01,500 --> 01:13:04,300
that would eventually into his
wisecracking partner, Blake.

2336
01:13:04,300 --> 01:13:05,933
- Oh, now, you're
just showing off.

2337
01:13:05,933 --> 01:13:07,100
- Hey, wait a minute.

2338
01:13:07,100 --> 01:13:08,600
Charles Darwin wasn't fictional.

2339
01:13:08,600 --> 01:13:09,933
- Just hush you two.

2340
01:13:09,933 --> 01:13:11,900
We've got commercials,
so let's go.

2341
01:13:11,900 --> 01:13:15,333
(light electronic music)

2342
01:13:17,933 --> 01:13:19,233
- [Crow] What kind of pet
would Space Ghost have?

2343
01:13:19,233 --> 01:13:20,200
- [Joel] Oh, that's a monkey.

2344
01:13:20,200 --> 01:13:21,133
- Oh yeah.

2345
01:13:21,133 --> 01:13:22,167
- [Tom] It's a trick question.

2346
01:13:22,167 --> 01:13:23,400
(grunting)

2347
01:13:23,400 --> 01:13:24,367
- You don't release Max
Keller until tomorrow.

2348
01:13:24,367 --> 01:13:25,833
- I thought he was your friend.

2349
01:13:25,833 --> 01:13:27,067
- He is.

2350
01:13:27,067 --> 01:13:28,433
But he'd insist
on going with us.

2351
01:13:28,433 --> 01:13:29,733
And I'm not getting him killed.

2352
01:13:29,733 --> 01:13:31,733
- [Tom] God, he bugs me.

2353
01:13:32,633 --> 01:13:33,567
- You got it.

2354
01:13:33,567 --> 01:13:34,700
- You got me!

2355
01:13:34,700 --> 01:13:36,467
- [Joel] Smug
brothers right there.

2356
01:13:36,467 --> 01:13:37,800
Couple of dorks.

2357
01:13:41,200 --> 01:13:42,800
Oh, he brought his sample case.

2358
01:13:42,800 --> 01:13:44,033
- [Tom] Yep.

2359
01:13:44,033 --> 01:13:44,900
- Well, no room
for underwear in--

2360
01:13:44,900 --> 01:13:46,233
- Sorry, Max.

2361
01:13:46,233 --> 01:13:47,233
- Yeah, all this stuff.

2362
01:13:47,233 --> 01:13:48,767
- This turns out
to be an ending,

2363
01:13:48,767 --> 01:13:50,700
wish we'd have
been together more.

2364
01:13:50,700 --> 01:13:52,100
- [Tom] Look at all
the things he can do

2365
01:13:52,100 --> 01:13:54,033
with his Spirograph.

2366
01:13:54,033 --> 01:13:55,500
- [Joel] Come along,
my little friend.

2367
01:13:55,500 --> 01:13:57,233
Even you, Longfellow.

2368
01:13:58,767 --> 01:14:00,733
- You know, his act
is kind of prop-heavy.

2369
01:14:00,733 --> 01:14:01,867
- [Joel] Yeah.

2370
01:14:01,867 --> 01:14:04,333
- [Joel] Uh, You
forgot your six finger.

2371
01:14:04,333 --> 01:14:05,833
- [Tom] Man alive.

2372
01:14:09,567 --> 01:14:11,733
(suspenseful synth music)

2373
01:14:11,733 --> 01:14:12,700
- The gerbil!

2374
01:14:12,700 --> 01:14:14,200
- [Tom] Oh no!

2375
01:14:14,200 --> 01:14:17,133
- [Joel] Wait, I thought
he turned that light off.

2376
01:14:17,133 --> 01:14:18,300
Sockies.

2377
01:14:18,300 --> 01:14:20,067
- Oh no, it's Queen
Latifah again.

2378
01:14:20,067 --> 01:14:21,800
- [Joel] You think
he just walked though

2379
01:14:21,800 --> 01:14:23,133
the lobby like that?

2380
01:14:23,133 --> 01:14:24,000
- [Tom] I don't know.

2381
01:14:24,000 --> 01:14:25,333
Music by Zamfir.

2382
01:14:27,767 --> 01:14:29,700
- Gotcha, you little Dickens.

2383
01:14:29,700 --> 01:14:31,933
(shouting)

2384
01:14:34,733 --> 01:14:36,467
- [Joel] It is
well choreographed.

2385
01:14:36,467 --> 01:14:38,200
- [Tom] Very nice.

2386
01:14:38,200 --> 01:14:40,633
- Everybody's going out for it.

2387
01:14:40,633 --> 01:14:41,700
- [Joel] Ooh!

2388
01:14:42,733 --> 01:14:44,000
(imitating knocking)

2389
01:14:44,000 --> 01:14:44,933
- [Tom] Hey, keep
it down in there.

2390
01:14:44,933 --> 01:14:46,600
Hey, I'm trying to sleep.

2391
01:14:46,600 --> 01:14:48,033
Shut up in there.

2392
01:14:49,800 --> 01:14:51,333
(shouting)

2393
01:14:51,333 --> 01:14:54,133
- [Joel] I don't think Lee
can take much more of this.

2394
01:14:54,133 --> 01:14:56,533
- [Tom] You know, I
don't think that's Lee.

2395
01:14:56,533 --> 01:14:58,133
- [Joel] I know.

2396
01:14:58,133 --> 01:14:59,600
(laughing)

2397
01:14:59,600 --> 01:15:00,767
- [Man] You betrayed us, Master.

2398
01:15:00,767 --> 01:15:02,667
- I get the bed by the window.

2399
01:15:02,667 --> 01:15:05,400
- [Man] Not without a weapon.

2400
01:15:05,400 --> 01:15:08,067
- [Tom] Oh, they do this every
episode, for crying out loud.

2401
01:15:08,067 --> 01:15:08,933
- [Joel] Ah!

2402
01:15:08,933 --> 01:15:10,200
That always happens.

2403
01:15:10,200 --> 01:15:11,467
- That's got to sting.

2404
01:15:11,467 --> 01:15:13,833
- [Tom] This guy's got a
knife in his didgeridoo.

2405
01:15:13,833 --> 01:15:16,600
(imitating didgeridoo)

2406
01:15:16,600 --> 01:15:18,233
Wilkinson sword.

2407
01:15:18,233 --> 01:15:20,500
(shouting)

2408
01:15:22,433 --> 01:15:27,033
- I bet Holiday Inn has a
policy on this kind of stuff.

2409
01:15:28,933 --> 01:15:31,367
- [Tom] Oh, I see you're
using the Danish counter.

2410
01:15:31,367 --> 01:15:35,200
I thought it was wise
considering the terrain.

2411
01:15:36,333 --> 01:15:38,600
(grunting)

2412
01:15:44,967 --> 01:15:46,700
Garden weasel!

2413
01:15:46,700 --> 01:15:49,533
- [Joel] Bruce Lee
Press-On Nails.

2414
01:15:51,333 --> 01:15:53,167
- Ooh, that's a punch.

2415
01:15:56,867 --> 01:15:58,100
- [Joel] Oh, man.

2416
01:15:58,100 --> 01:15:59,933
And Designing Women
is on in half an hour.

2417
01:15:59,933 --> 01:16:01,000
- [Tom] Damn.

2418
01:16:06,000 --> 01:16:09,700
- Oh, I've heard about
this kind of behavior.

2419
01:16:09,700 --> 01:16:10,567
- [Tom] Jump back.

2420
01:16:10,567 --> 01:16:11,667
Erase myself.

2421
01:16:12,900 --> 01:16:13,800
- [Tom] Oh, weak,

2422
01:16:13,800 --> 01:16:14,633
(booing)

2423
01:16:14,633 --> 01:16:16,133
Weak, weak.

2424
01:16:16,133 --> 01:16:18,000
- [Joel] I'm starting to not
believe this ninja stuff.

2425
01:16:18,000 --> 01:16:19,400
- Where has my little dog gone?

2426
01:16:19,400 --> 01:16:20,400
- [Tom] Arf.

2427
01:16:21,367 --> 01:16:22,567
- You know?

2428
01:16:22,567 --> 01:16:24,333
- [Max] They had to
release me. No evidence.

2429
01:16:24,333 --> 01:16:25,467
Now I had to get to the Master.

2430
01:16:25,467 --> 01:16:26,633
- [Joel] I'm innocent.

2431
01:16:26,633 --> 01:16:29,133
He soldered me in here, help.

2432
01:16:29,133 --> 01:16:30,367
- I know why he did it.

2433
01:16:30,367 --> 01:16:32,033
But he's not getting
away with it.

2434
01:16:32,033 --> 01:16:33,533
- [Tom] With what?

2435
01:16:36,133 --> 01:16:37,233
So, cow flop?

2436
01:16:41,167 --> 01:16:42,667
- Do you think they'll find us?

2437
01:16:42,667 --> 01:16:43,833
- Nice caftan.

2438
01:16:44,833 --> 01:16:46,067
- Really?

2439
01:16:46,067 --> 01:16:47,300
- Yes, they will.

2440
01:16:47,300 --> 01:16:48,767
- [Tom] Have a cow flop.

2441
01:16:48,767 --> 01:16:52,767
- [Joel] Let Hostage House
cater your next caper.

2442
01:16:52,767 --> 01:16:53,833
- [Tom] Please,
it's Shake 'n Bake.

2443
01:16:53,833 --> 01:16:55,000
And we helped.

2444
01:16:57,167 --> 01:16:58,033
- Come on.

2445
01:16:58,033 --> 01:16:58,867
Its original recipe.

2446
01:16:58,867 --> 01:16:59,700
Eat.

2447
01:17:01,767 --> 01:17:03,400
- [Tom] I'm missing
All My Children.

2448
01:17:03,400 --> 01:17:04,400
(crying)

2449
01:17:04,400 --> 01:17:06,400
- [Tom] Come on,
everybody, sing.

2450
01:17:06,400 --> 01:17:08,600
♪ Get a bucket of chicken. ♪

2451
01:17:08,600 --> 01:17:09,433
- [Joel] Come on.

2452
01:17:09,433 --> 01:17:11,133
♪ Finger lick-- ♪

2453
01:17:11,133 --> 01:17:13,733
- Boy, this chicken's
just no going over.

2454
01:17:13,733 --> 01:17:15,333
- [Tom] Aw, hell, I'm not shy.

2455
01:17:15,333 --> 01:17:17,733
Can I have your dessert, too?

2456
01:17:19,200 --> 01:17:20,033
Hm?

2457
01:17:22,600 --> 01:17:23,433
- [Joel] It's the Colonel!

2458
01:17:23,433 --> 01:17:24,267
(gasping)

2459
01:17:24,267 --> 01:17:26,733
- [Alicia] John Palin?

2460
01:17:26,733 --> 01:17:28,667
- [Joel] Sit down.

2461
01:17:28,667 --> 01:17:31,667
- Now why didn't
you eat my chicken?

2462
01:17:31,667 --> 01:17:32,667
- John.

2463
01:17:32,667 --> 01:17:34,167
- [Tom] Marsha.

2464
01:17:34,167 --> 01:17:35,533
- You're one of them.

2465
01:17:35,533 --> 01:17:37,033
- Poor little rich girl.

2466
01:17:37,033 --> 01:17:38,400
- [Joel] The Gloria
Vanderbilt story.

2467
01:17:38,400 --> 01:17:41,300
- You're not so beautiful
and defiant now.

2468
01:17:41,300 --> 01:17:43,067
- [Tom] Well, she's
still defiant.

2469
01:17:43,067 --> 01:17:45,900
(laughing)

2470
01:17:45,900 --> 01:17:47,300
- I could kill you right now.

2471
01:17:47,300 --> 01:17:48,467
- You're going to
kill us anyway,

2472
01:17:48,467 --> 01:17:49,667
and don't you think
we all know it

2473
01:17:49,667 --> 01:17:50,900
- [Joel] Zing.

2474
01:17:50,900 --> 01:17:53,200
- No one's coming
for you, Alicia.

2475
01:17:53,200 --> 01:17:54,133
- There.

2476
01:17:54,133 --> 01:17:56,267
I've said it and I'm proud.

2477
01:17:57,133 --> 01:17:58,133
- [Joel] Ken Berry.

2478
01:17:58,133 --> 01:17:58,967
Huh.

2479
01:18:01,400 --> 01:18:04,800
- [Tom] Boy, rotten
senior trip, eh, honey?

2480
01:18:04,800 --> 01:18:05,633
- Max.

2481
01:18:06,500 --> 01:18:09,367
(suspenseful orchestral music)

2482
01:18:09,367 --> 01:18:10,267
- It hurts.

2483
01:18:11,467 --> 01:18:13,367
- Going to need me.

2484
01:18:13,367 --> 01:18:15,533
But thanks for the sentiment.

2485
01:18:15,533 --> 01:18:19,633
- [Tom] You ever see
Food of the Gods, buddy?

2486
01:18:19,633 --> 01:18:20,467
(owl hooting)

2487
01:18:20,467 --> 01:18:23,300
(imitating owl hooting)

2488
01:18:23,300 --> 01:18:24,800
- This is it.

2489
01:18:24,800 --> 01:18:27,333
- Well, you're in it
now, up to your neck.

2490
01:18:27,333 --> 01:18:28,933
- I don't like trusting you.

2491
01:18:28,933 --> 01:18:31,667
- [Lee] I don't think
you have much choice.

2492
01:18:31,667 --> 01:18:32,900
- [Joel] Zinged him.

2493
01:18:32,900 --> 01:18:36,000
- [Lee] You climb as
I do, or you'll fall.

2494
01:18:40,267 --> 01:18:41,200
- Hi-keeba.

2495
01:18:47,400 --> 01:18:50,333
- [Tom] Huh, so he's
climbing a silo.

2496
01:18:50,333 --> 01:18:51,367
- [Max] Found out
about the fortress

2497
01:18:51,367 --> 01:18:52,500
in the federal building.

2498
01:18:52,500 --> 01:18:53,300
- [Joel] And the
digger, and the dealer,

2499
01:18:53,300 --> 01:18:54,800
and the dog as well.

2500
01:18:54,800 --> 01:18:57,533
- [Max] And getting in there
were two different things.

2501
01:18:57,533 --> 01:19:00,333
(light horn music)

2502
01:19:00,333 --> 01:19:04,000
- Hey, sounds like Chicago's
in the back of the van.

2503
01:19:04,000 --> 01:19:06,333
- [Tom] Hey, crack a window.

2504
01:19:11,367 --> 01:19:12,633
- Great night for flying.

2505
01:19:12,633 --> 01:19:15,333
- [Joel] Uh, Flying on
the ground is wrong.

2506
01:19:15,333 --> 01:19:17,900
- [Tom] You get up
that rope, Seeger.

2507
01:19:17,900 --> 01:19:20,267
- Oh, the great Master
Ninja needs a spotter.

2508
01:19:20,267 --> 01:19:21,267
- [Tom] Uh-oh.

2509
01:19:21,267 --> 01:19:22,133
(gasping)

2510
01:19:22,133 --> 01:19:23,633
- [Joel] Reaction.

2511
01:19:28,400 --> 01:19:30,367
- Cripes, I wet them.

2512
01:19:30,367 --> 01:19:32,033
Look out down there.

2513
01:19:34,300 --> 01:19:35,400
- [Tom] Stay together, cheeks.

2514
01:19:35,400 --> 01:19:37,067
Stay together, cheeks.

2515
01:19:37,067 --> 01:19:37,900
Ooh.

2516
01:19:41,567 --> 01:19:43,333
- Where does he get
this stuff from?

2517
01:19:43,333 --> 01:19:44,833
- [Joel] You know.

2518
01:19:46,100 --> 01:19:46,933
Reaction.

2519
01:19:48,800 --> 01:19:50,367
- [Tom] Oh brother.

2520
01:19:52,767 --> 01:19:54,700
Uh, off belay, sort of.

2521
01:19:56,133 --> 01:19:56,967
Uh, there.

2522
01:19:56,967 --> 01:19:58,433
- Ah.

2523
01:19:58,433 --> 01:19:59,833
- [Joel] Watch, now as
they go up the roof,

2524
01:19:59,833 --> 01:20:01,633
a celebrity will
stick his head out.

2525
01:20:01,633 --> 01:20:02,767
- Yeah.

2526
01:20:02,767 --> 01:20:04,100
- [Joel] Batman.

2527
01:20:08,033 --> 01:20:09,433
- [Tom] Prime it.

2528
01:20:11,433 --> 01:20:12,700
Where did he get this thing?

2529
01:20:12,700 --> 01:20:15,467
What is he, Hudson Hawk?

2530
01:20:15,467 --> 01:20:16,767
- First-pull start.

2531
01:20:16,767 --> 01:20:17,967
Starts every time.

2532
01:20:17,967 --> 01:20:18,967
- [Tom] Huh.

2533
01:20:25,300 --> 01:20:26,700
- Lean back, Tim.

2534
01:20:30,833 --> 01:20:31,833
- [Joel] Well, if old
fatty up there can do it,

2535
01:20:31,833 --> 01:20:33,500
I guess I can.

2536
01:20:33,500 --> 01:20:38,500
- [Tom] Looks like he's
climbing a rosary, doesn't it?

2537
01:20:39,933 --> 01:20:43,600
- I get a weird feeling
when I shimmy up this rope.

2538
01:20:44,233 --> 01:20:44,800
- [Tom] Ator?

2539
01:20:44,800 --> 01:20:45,367
No!

2540
01:20:47,767 --> 01:20:49,300
- Quiet, Tim.

2541
01:20:49,300 --> 01:20:50,567
Shh.

2542
01:20:50,567 --> 01:20:51,700
- Picture yourself over
the Sea of Japan, Max.

2543
01:20:51,700 --> 01:20:53,200
- [Tom] Auguring in.

2544
01:20:53,200 --> 01:20:56,133
- Did he bring his
hamster on the ultralight?

2545
01:20:56,133 --> 01:20:56,967
- [Joel] No, he's
talking to himself.

2546
01:20:56,967 --> 01:20:57,767
- Oh.

2547
01:21:04,533 --> 01:21:05,633
- Follow me.

2548
01:21:05,633 --> 01:21:07,100
Keep your balance.

2549
01:21:07,100 --> 01:21:09,000
- I know how to balance.

2550
01:21:09,000 --> 01:21:10,133
- Duh, I'm sure.

2551
01:21:10,133 --> 01:21:11,233
- Then keep your voice down.

2552
01:21:11,233 --> 01:21:12,133
- [Tom] What?

2553
01:21:12,133 --> 01:21:12,967
Oh, voice down.

2554
01:21:12,967 --> 01:21:13,867
Shh, right.

2555
01:21:15,367 --> 01:21:16,833
- [Joel] Come on.

2556
01:21:16,833 --> 01:21:20,033
Hurry, I've got to get
this tux back to Gingiss.

2557
01:21:20,033 --> 01:21:21,567
- [Lee] Come on.

2558
01:21:21,567 --> 01:21:22,533
- [Man] What's the plan?

2559
01:21:22,533 --> 01:21:23,367
- [Tom] Plan?

2560
01:21:23,367 --> 01:21:24,200
Oh, oh.

2561
01:21:24,200 --> 01:21:25,133
- [Lee] Split up.

2562
01:21:25,133 --> 01:21:26,167
Back at this wall in 20 minutes.

2563
01:21:26,167 --> 01:21:27,733
- [Man] You got it.

2564
01:21:28,900 --> 01:21:30,100
- [Serena] Two of them, huh?

2565
01:21:30,100 --> 01:21:30,933
- Shoot them down.

2566
01:21:30,933 --> 01:21:31,767
Shoot to kill.

2567
01:21:31,767 --> 01:21:33,300
- Too late, Mr. Mallory.

2568
01:21:33,300 --> 01:21:35,200
This time, you're too late.

2569
01:21:35,200 --> 01:21:36,200
- [Tom] Whoa, wait.

2570
01:21:36,200 --> 01:21:37,700
We missed something again.

2571
01:21:37,700 --> 01:21:38,967
- Wow, he landed in a cistern.

2572
01:21:38,967 --> 01:21:40,833
- [Joel] We now join
Timothy Van Patten,

2573
01:21:40,833 --> 01:21:43,167
already in progress.

2574
01:21:43,167 --> 01:21:46,000
(imitating music)

2575
01:21:47,300 --> 01:21:48,200
- [Tom] Careful, Tim.

2576
01:21:48,200 --> 01:21:49,500
That could hurt.

2577
01:21:52,033 --> 01:21:53,867
- [Serena] Who is
this man, Mallory?

2578
01:21:53,867 --> 01:21:54,733
- An old enemy.

2579
01:21:54,733 --> 01:21:55,567
I'll take care of him.

2580
01:21:55,567 --> 01:21:56,533
- It's army class.

2581
01:21:56,533 --> 01:21:57,967
- Okay, thanks, Forbes.

2582
01:21:57,967 --> 01:21:59,067
Uh, thanks for the information.

2583
01:21:59,067 --> 01:22:00,367
I'll inform Senator Clayton.

2584
01:22:00,367 --> 01:22:01,467
- [Tom] Roger.

2585
01:22:01,467 --> 01:22:03,833
Thanks for your order.

2586
01:22:03,833 --> 01:22:05,733
- They're going to launch
a full-scale helicopter

2587
01:22:05,733 --> 01:22:07,767
assault at six o'clock.

2588
01:22:07,767 --> 01:22:09,000
- Could they be mistaken?

2589
01:22:09,000 --> 01:22:10,533
- They have no
reason to lie to me.

2590
01:22:10,533 --> 01:22:12,500
The helicopters are standing
at the foot of the mountain,

2591
01:22:12,500 --> 01:22:13,633
waiting to go.

2592
01:22:13,633 --> 01:22:14,933
We haven't got any time,

2593
01:22:14,933 --> 01:22:16,833
unless you intend
to stand and fight.

2594
01:22:16,833 --> 01:22:18,367
- That's something else
he gave a long time ago.

2595
01:22:18,367 --> 01:22:19,200
- [Tom] Woof.

2596
01:22:19,200 --> 01:22:20,433
- I know when to fight.

2597
01:22:20,433 --> 01:22:21,867
When our back's
against the wall.

2598
01:22:21,867 --> 01:22:24,333
We can be out of here
in under an hour.

2599
01:22:24,333 --> 01:22:25,400
Get everything ready.

2600
01:22:25,400 --> 01:22:26,233
- [Tom] Debbie Do-Right.

2601
01:22:26,233 --> 01:22:27,467
- The hostages?

2602
01:22:27,467 --> 01:22:28,900
- We'll execute them
just before we leave.

2603
01:22:28,900 --> 01:22:30,533
- Oh, you always put everything
off till the last minute.

2604
01:22:30,533 --> 01:22:32,633
- Your cause can
be served, Serena.

2605
01:22:32,633 --> 01:22:34,700
Next time, they'll listen.

2606
01:22:34,700 --> 01:22:38,967
- [Joel] Oh, uh, Dave,
Shaggy wants his beard back.

2607
01:22:42,067 --> 01:22:43,900
- [Tom] I think someone
could stand to sober up.

2608
01:22:43,900 --> 01:22:46,067
Take a shave and a shower.

2609
01:22:46,067 --> 01:22:46,900
- [Joel] Hi, Chet.

2610
01:22:46,900 --> 01:22:48,167
- How's it going, Doris?

2611
01:22:48,167 --> 01:22:49,000
- [Joel] Oh, fine.

2612
01:22:49,000 --> 01:22:50,200
- Hmm, not bad.

2613
01:22:50,200 --> 01:22:52,233
- [Tom] Owie ow ow ow.

2614
01:22:52,233 --> 01:22:53,300
Spock, Spock.

2615
01:22:54,700 --> 01:22:55,533
- [Lee] Where?

2616
01:22:55,533 --> 01:22:56,400
- Over there.

2617
01:22:56,400 --> 01:22:57,800
Restin tower.

2618
01:22:57,800 --> 01:22:58,633
- [Tom] Okey-doke.

2619
01:22:58,633 --> 01:22:59,600
Thanks a lot

2620
01:23:01,467 --> 01:23:03,967
- Lee's the butt of that joke.

2621
01:23:05,833 --> 01:23:07,100
- [Tom] Hey, A Shot in the Dark.

2622
01:23:07,100 --> 01:23:08,833
- Your government cares
nothing for your lives.

2623
01:23:08,833 --> 01:23:10,967
They're the ones executing you.

2624
01:23:10,967 --> 01:23:13,767
- [Joel] I wouldn't
pay my taxes either.

2625
01:23:13,767 --> 01:23:15,733
- Poor little rich
girl is getting first--

2626
01:23:15,733 --> 01:23:17,233
- [Alicia] Oh no.

2627
01:23:17,233 --> 01:23:19,400
- [Tom] Boy, her dress is
taking a beating, isn't it?

2628
01:23:19,400 --> 01:23:20,967
- [Joel] No one follows us.

2629
01:23:20,967 --> 01:23:22,900
I know what you said about
my skull and I blew up.

2630
01:23:22,900 --> 01:23:24,600
Well, I'm just leaving.

2631
01:23:24,600 --> 01:23:25,800
- Gee, they seemed nice.

2632
01:23:25,800 --> 01:23:28,133
- Everything's going
to be all right.

2633
01:23:28,133 --> 01:23:30,300
- [Tom] Hey, look,
a furnace filter.

2634
01:23:30,300 --> 01:23:32,333
(humming)

2635
01:23:32,333 --> 01:23:33,700
- [Tom] It's not
funny, you know.

2636
01:23:33,700 --> 01:23:35,800
It's a furnace filter.

2637
01:23:35,800 --> 01:23:36,633
- Freeze!

2638
01:23:36,633 --> 01:23:37,833
- Tag!

2639
01:23:37,833 --> 01:23:39,133
Not it.
- Don't even think about it.

2640
01:23:39,133 --> 01:23:42,567
(light electronic music)

2641
01:23:46,667 --> 01:23:47,500
- Senator.

2642
01:23:47,500 --> 01:23:48,700
(all yelling)

2643
01:23:48,700 --> 01:23:49,933
- You said something
about a backup.

2644
01:23:49,933 --> 01:23:51,233
- It's a longshot, Senator.

2645
01:23:51,233 --> 01:23:52,533
- [Tom] It's a tape backup.

2646
01:23:52,533 --> 01:23:54,633
You're leaning on it.

2647
01:23:54,633 --> 01:23:57,800
- The assault force is ready.

2648
01:23:57,800 --> 01:23:58,767
- You heard from Mallory?

2649
01:23:58,767 --> 01:23:59,867
- [Joel] No, no word. no.

2650
01:23:59,867 --> 01:24:01,467
- What about McAllister?

2651
01:24:01,467 --> 01:24:02,400
They could have got separated.

2652
01:24:02,400 --> 01:24:03,533
- Monitoring both frequencies.

2653
01:24:03,533 --> 01:24:04,367
Nothing.

2654
01:24:04,367 --> 01:24:05,300
- [Tom] Nothing, huh?

2655
01:24:05,300 --> 01:24:06,100
Too bad.

2656
01:24:06,100 --> 01:24:06,933
- Send them in.

2657
01:24:06,933 --> 01:24:07,767
- Sorry.

2658
01:24:09,200 --> 01:24:10,433
- [Joel] Lose the tux, will you?

2659
01:24:10,433 --> 01:24:11,833
It's starting to
smell like Fritos.

2660
01:24:11,833 --> 01:24:13,633
- I got a headache this big.

2661
01:24:13,633 --> 01:24:14,900
- [Joel] Oh, my aching neck.

2662
01:24:14,900 --> 01:24:17,667
Second under, what are,
what are you looking at?

2663
01:24:17,667 --> 01:24:19,367
- We've seen it. It's a
nice piece of real estate.

2664
01:24:19,367 --> 01:24:20,567
We know!

2665
01:24:20,567 --> 01:24:22,167
- We put him in here.

2666
01:24:22,167 --> 01:24:23,967
He was wearing some kind
of black ninja outfit.

2667
01:24:23,967 --> 01:24:24,933
- [Tom] Real dopey looking.

2668
01:24:24,933 --> 01:24:25,767
- He's gone.

2669
01:24:25,767 --> 01:24:27,300
- [All] Huh?

2670
01:24:27,300 --> 01:24:28,233
(suspenseful jazz music)

2671
01:24:28,233 --> 01:24:30,100
- And this time, it's personal.

2672
01:24:30,100 --> 01:24:31,800
- [Joel] Ow, right on my keys.

2673
01:24:31,800 --> 01:24:32,633
Ow.

2674
01:24:34,567 --> 01:24:36,133
- [Tom] My mask.

2675
01:24:36,133 --> 01:24:37,033
Time Tunnel.

2676
01:24:37,033 --> 01:24:38,167
In color.

2677
01:24:38,167 --> 01:24:40,667
(whistling)

2678
01:24:40,667 --> 01:24:43,067
(imitating music)

2679
01:24:43,067 --> 01:24:45,700
- [Joel] Hey, the Average
White Band's up there.

2680
01:24:45,700 --> 01:24:46,933
- [John] Sit down, Alicia.

2681
01:24:46,933 --> 01:24:48,500
- So I guess I'll
sit here then, okay?

2682
01:24:48,500 --> 01:24:49,333
Guy.

2683
01:24:54,900 --> 01:24:58,167
- [Tom] How long have
I had split ends?

2684
01:24:59,267 --> 01:25:00,133
Hey.

2685
01:25:00,133 --> 01:25:01,367
- Hey!

2686
01:25:01,367 --> 01:25:03,000
- Let's see how
brave you are now.

2687
01:25:03,000 --> 01:25:05,267
- Gip your hang off of her.

2688
01:25:07,033 --> 01:25:10,267
- [Tom] A stunt double
all of a sudden.

2689
01:25:12,533 --> 01:25:13,733
My.

2690
01:25:13,733 --> 01:25:15,800
- [Joel] You really
slide on that linoleum.

2691
01:25:15,800 --> 01:25:16,767
- Alicia, are you okay?

2692
01:25:16,767 --> 01:25:18,300
- [Alicia] Oh, yes.

2693
01:25:18,300 --> 01:25:20,200
- It's your breath.

2694
01:25:20,200 --> 01:25:21,033
- Max!

2695
01:25:21,033 --> 01:25:23,167
(all yelling)

2696
01:25:23,167 --> 01:25:24,533
- [Tom] Oh.

2697
01:25:24,533 --> 01:25:26,200
The end.
- [Lee] Are you all right?

2698
01:25:26,200 --> 01:25:27,467
- I'm okay.

2699
01:25:27,467 --> 01:25:29,233
- I don't even want
to how you got here.

2700
01:25:29,233 --> 01:25:30,100
- Sea of Japan.

2701
01:25:30,100 --> 01:25:30,933
Glided in.

2702
01:25:30,933 --> 01:25:31,867
You know how that is.

2703
01:25:31,867 --> 01:25:33,067
What's happened to Mallory?

2704
01:25:33,067 --> 01:25:34,467
Little tete-a-tete
with Castile--

2705
01:25:34,467 --> 01:25:35,300
- Tater tots?

2706
01:25:35,300 --> 01:25:36,367
- [Tom] Mm.

2707
01:25:36,367 --> 01:25:38,100
- Should buy us enough time.

2708
01:25:38,100 --> 01:25:40,267
- If it's any help, there's
an arsenal in the garage.

2709
01:25:40,267 --> 01:25:41,600
and, uh--

2710
01:25:41,600 --> 01:25:43,367
- [Tom] Ocelot?
- Not until I put this back.

2711
01:25:43,367 --> 01:25:45,300
- [Joel] Hey, an RF
cable. Thanks, Tim.

2712
01:25:45,300 --> 01:25:47,233
- There's a guard on the door
at the top of the stairs.

2713
01:25:47,233 --> 01:25:48,433
Is that where the rest
of the hostages are?

2714
01:25:48,433 --> 01:25:49,367
- Yeah.

2715
01:25:49,367 --> 01:25:50,800
- [Tom] Don't feed them chicken.

2716
01:25:50,800 --> 01:25:51,733
- Get your truck ready.

2717
01:25:51,733 --> 01:25:52,700
Make sure the gates are open.

2718
01:25:52,700 --> 01:25:53,567
I need your help.

2719
01:25:53,567 --> 01:25:54,633
- To do what?

2720
01:25:54,633 --> 01:25:55,467
- Scream.

2721
01:25:55,467 --> 01:25:56,300
- [Tom] Pull my finger.

2722
01:25:56,300 --> 01:25:57,133
- What?

2723
01:25:57,133 --> 01:25:57,967
- [Both] Scream.

2724
01:25:57,967 --> 01:25:59,167
(screaming)

2725
01:25:59,167 --> 01:26:00,067
- [Joel] Good.

2726
01:26:00,067 --> 01:26:01,167
That's my cue.

2727
01:26:02,733 --> 01:26:03,733
- [Tom] Alley-oop.

2728
01:26:03,733 --> 01:26:05,133
Give and go.

2729
01:26:05,133 --> 01:26:06,033
- Appreciate the help.

2730
01:26:06,033 --> 01:26:06,900
- Any time.

2731
01:26:06,900 --> 01:26:08,033
- Listen, pal.

2732
01:26:08,033 --> 01:26:09,533
- Pull my finger.

2733
01:26:09,533 --> 01:26:11,267
- You're starting to look
more like me every day.

2734
01:26:11,267 --> 01:26:12,833
I must be rubbing off on you.

2735
01:26:12,833 --> 01:26:14,500
- [Joel] Ew, ick.
- I said pull my finger.

2736
01:26:14,500 --> 01:26:15,833
Ah, he's not going to do it.

2737
01:26:15,833 --> 01:26:17,000
Come on.

2738
01:26:17,000 --> 01:26:18,200
- [Tom] Suddenly
she's a ninja groupie.

2739
01:26:18,200 --> 01:26:20,533
Don't hang around with them.

2740
01:26:21,867 --> 01:26:24,533
- [Joel] This is a ninja cookie.

2741
01:26:25,833 --> 01:26:26,667
Stand straight like a soldier.

2742
01:26:26,667 --> 01:26:27,500
(bomb lightly exploding)

2743
01:26:27,500 --> 01:26:29,400
- Oh, I'm, like, blind.

2744
01:26:32,000 --> 01:26:33,000
(screaming)

2745
01:26:33,000 --> 01:26:34,467
- Quiet!

2746
01:26:34,467 --> 01:26:35,000
- [Tom] Whoa, omebody
let a crow loose in here?

2747
01:26:35,000 --> 01:26:35,667
Shut up!

2748
01:26:35,667 --> 01:26:36,433
- Everybody.

2749
01:26:36,433 --> 01:26:37,267
Don't be afraid.

2750
01:26:37,267 --> 01:26:38,100
Get out.

2751
01:26:38,100 --> 01:26:39,367
Come on.

2752
01:26:39,367 --> 01:26:40,867
You're on your way,
you're on your way.

2753
01:26:40,867 --> 01:26:43,800
- [Joel] Hurry up, my parents
will be home in 10 minutes.

2754
01:26:43,800 --> 01:26:45,900
- Sure hope somebody
grabbed that chicken.

2755
01:26:45,900 --> 01:26:47,833
- Move it, come on.

2756
01:26:47,833 --> 01:26:50,167
- [Joel] Mom said, never
trust a guy in satin.

2757
01:26:50,167 --> 01:26:51,000
- [Tom] You cad!

2758
01:26:51,000 --> 01:26:51,833
Grrr.

2759
01:26:53,533 --> 01:26:54,367
- Start the executions.

2760
01:26:54,367 --> 01:26:55,300
- [Joel] Without me.

2761
01:26:55,300 --> 01:26:56,133
(imitating rimshot)

2762
01:26:56,133 --> 01:26:57,667
- Load the helicopters.

2763
01:26:57,667 --> 01:27:00,067
Mr. Mallory and I have a few
quiet words to say together.

2764
01:27:00,067 --> 01:27:00,967
In private.

2765
01:27:00,967 --> 01:27:02,033
(gasping)

2766
01:27:02,033 --> 01:27:03,067
- [Tom] Say.

2767
01:27:03,067 --> 01:27:04,567
- [Castile] Don't.

2768
01:27:04,567 --> 01:27:06,033
- [Tom] No, don't move.

2769
01:27:06,033 --> 01:27:07,900
I want to remember you
just as you are right now.

2770
01:27:07,900 --> 01:27:09,233
- Getting rattled?

2771
01:27:09,233 --> 01:27:11,300
A little
uncharacteristic emotion.

2772
01:27:11,300 --> 01:27:12,567
- I'm hammered.

2773
01:27:12,567 --> 01:27:14,033
- You've killed a
lot of my friends.

2774
01:27:14,033 --> 01:27:14,867
- [Tom] So?

2775
01:27:14,867 --> 01:27:15,800
- Got in the way.

2776
01:27:15,800 --> 01:27:17,300
I don't kill innocent people.

2777
01:27:17,300 --> 01:27:19,433
- What about your control,
sending in his assault force?

2778
01:27:19,433 --> 01:27:21,300
You think he cares about
the lives of the hostages?

2779
01:27:21,300 --> 01:27:23,833
- All he cares about
is stopping terrorism.

2780
01:27:23,833 --> 01:27:25,500
- It's all terrorism.

2781
01:27:25,500 --> 01:27:27,467
Different names,
different causes.

2782
01:27:27,467 --> 01:27:28,333
- [Tom] Ooh, deep.

2783
01:27:28,333 --> 01:27:29,200
- Save the world.

2784
01:27:29,200 --> 01:27:30,833
For what?

2785
01:27:30,833 --> 01:27:32,567
What do you care about, Mallory?

2786
01:27:32,567 --> 01:27:34,100
- David's got a little
pain to work through.

2787
01:27:34,100 --> 01:27:35,300
- [Joel] Yeah, I think so.

2788
01:27:35,300 --> 01:27:36,233
- Oh, I see.

2789
01:27:36,233 --> 01:27:37,400
You're being professional.

2790
01:27:37,400 --> 01:27:38,667
Using whatever time's
left to reflect

2791
01:27:38,667 --> 01:27:41,633
on the cost of your
professionalism.

2792
01:27:41,633 --> 01:27:43,033
- I'm Max Keller.

2793
01:27:43,033 --> 01:27:43,867
Cripes.

2794
01:27:43,867 --> 01:27:44,867
Where'd I park my van?

2795
01:27:44,867 --> 01:27:46,100
- [Tom] Hey what
happened to him?

2796
01:27:46,100 --> 01:27:47,833
- [Joel] Took a bullet
in the flipper, I think.

2797
01:27:47,833 --> 01:27:49,933
- [Tom] Guess so.

2798
01:27:49,933 --> 01:27:52,367
- This place is really swell.

2799
01:27:54,133 --> 01:27:54,967
- [Max] Uh-oh.

2800
01:27:54,967 --> 01:27:56,200
- [Tom] Oh, wrong door.

2801
01:27:56,200 --> 01:27:58,067
Oh man, oh man, oh
man, oh man, oh man.

2802
01:27:58,067 --> 01:27:59,433
- [Joel] Blondes have more guns.

2803
01:27:59,433 --> 01:28:01,867
(gun firing)

2804
01:28:01,867 --> 01:28:03,533
My Thom McCans!

2805
01:28:03,533 --> 01:28:05,133
- [Tom] Now, the willie.

2806
01:28:05,133 --> 01:28:06,267
- You're going to be last.

2807
01:28:06,267 --> 01:28:09,233
(gun firing)

2808
01:28:09,233 --> 01:28:10,433
- Huzzah!

2809
01:28:10,433 --> 01:28:11,833
(laughing)

2810
01:28:11,833 --> 01:28:13,533
- [Joel] Oh, now he's into that.

2811
01:28:13,533 --> 01:28:14,767
(coughing)

2812
01:28:14,767 --> 01:28:16,333
- [Tom] So why doesn't
the gas affect him?

2813
01:28:16,333 --> 01:28:19,333
- He can't breathe
through his nose.

2814
01:28:21,633 --> 01:28:24,200
♪ What goes up ♪

2815
01:28:27,200 --> 01:28:28,033
(gun firing)

2816
01:28:28,033 --> 01:28:28,867
- [Joel] That was me.

2817
01:28:28,867 --> 01:28:30,300
Sorry.

2818
01:28:30,300 --> 01:28:32,133
- I'd say the marines
have just landed.

2819
01:28:32,133 --> 01:28:34,800
- Too late to help you, Mallory.

2820
01:28:35,833 --> 01:28:37,500
- Ha ha, silly String!

2821
01:28:37,500 --> 01:28:38,933
Whoo hoo, huzzah!

2822
01:28:41,800 --> 01:28:42,733
- Who are you?

2823
01:28:42,733 --> 01:28:43,567
- [Lee] You'll never know.

2824
01:28:43,567 --> 01:28:46,033
♪ Just how much I ♪

2825
01:28:46,033 --> 01:28:47,900
- [Joel] Gymkata.

2826
01:28:47,900 --> 01:28:49,400
- [Tom] Good move.

2827
01:28:53,067 --> 01:28:54,300
- Well, thanks.

2828
01:28:55,667 --> 01:28:57,133
That was nice work.
- [Tom] If you can get it.

2829
01:28:57,133 --> 01:28:59,167
- Max is loading the
hostages onto a truck.

2830
01:28:59,167 --> 01:29:01,700
Now let's get out of here.

2831
01:29:01,700 --> 01:29:04,367
- Ryder rents, loser transports.

2832
01:29:07,300 --> 01:29:09,533
(grunting)

2833
01:29:18,067 --> 01:29:19,867
Hey, you got our stuff.

2834
01:29:19,867 --> 01:29:21,300
(suspenseful flute music)

2835
01:29:21,300 --> 01:29:23,467
(imitating flute)

2836
01:29:23,467 --> 01:29:24,567
Oh, yes.

2837
01:29:24,567 --> 01:29:25,467
I love these shots.

2838
01:29:25,467 --> 01:29:26,500
Slow it down more.

2839
01:29:26,500 --> 01:29:27,333
Please.

2840
01:29:27,333 --> 01:29:28,667
- [Tom] Hi-Keeba

2841
01:29:30,467 --> 01:29:32,400
- [Joel] Now it looks like
they're climbing down a rosary.

2842
01:29:32,400 --> 01:29:33,400
- [Tom] Yup.

2843
01:29:35,267 --> 01:29:36,100
- Ow, ooh.

2844
01:29:38,467 --> 01:29:40,233
It's the knots that, ouch.

2845
01:29:40,233 --> 01:29:41,500
Oh, rope burns.

2846
01:29:51,900 --> 01:29:54,833
- [Tom] Now, let's
go home, friend.

2847
01:29:58,233 --> 01:29:59,067
- Ow.

2848
01:29:59,067 --> 01:30:00,300
Be careful, I'm wealthy.

2849
01:30:00,300 --> 01:30:02,167
- [Joel] I don't think
U-Haul recommends that.

2850
01:30:02,167 --> 01:30:04,833
- [Tom] The migrant
socialites, bound for Malibu.

2851
01:30:04,833 --> 01:30:08,400
- Uh, will you
guys be my friend?

2852
01:30:08,400 --> 01:30:09,633
- [Joel] Whoa there,
just a little bit.

2853
01:30:09,633 --> 01:30:11,100
Huh.

2854
01:30:11,100 --> 01:30:12,933
- Yeah, he's a ninja, all right.
Look at the cat-like moves.

2855
01:30:12,933 --> 01:30:15,967
- So you came back for me.
- You'd have come back for me.

2856
01:30:15,967 --> 01:30:17,167
- I would now.

2857
01:30:17,167 --> 01:30:18,767
- [Joel] Ah, you
big lug, come here.

2858
01:30:18,767 --> 01:30:20,000
Ah.

2859
01:30:20,000 --> 01:30:21,300
- [Tom] His tux sure
held up well, huh?

2860
01:30:21,300 --> 01:30:23,300
- Didn't expect
to see you again.

2861
01:30:23,300 --> 01:30:25,267
- I had the same feeling
about you last night.

2862
01:30:25,267 --> 01:30:27,367
I should have known better.
- [Tom] With a girl like you.

2863
01:30:27,367 --> 01:30:28,300
- What can I do?

2864
01:30:28,300 --> 01:30:29,300
- Take a few less chances.

2865
01:30:29,300 --> 01:30:30,900
- I'll stop when you stop.

2866
01:30:30,900 --> 01:30:32,633
- One two three stop!

2867
01:30:36,300 --> 01:30:38,400
- [Tom] Oh, guests of Master
Ninja fly Air America.

2868
01:30:38,400 --> 01:30:41,367
- Glad they weren't early.

2869
01:30:41,367 --> 01:30:43,300
- One Adam-12, stop the movie.

2870
01:30:43,300 --> 01:30:44,133
- [Tom] Please.

2871
01:30:44,133 --> 01:30:45,667
- Once you're safe.

2872
01:30:45,667 --> 01:30:47,233
There'll be a bus to pick
you up here in a moment.

2873
01:30:47,233 --> 01:30:48,467
- [Joel] And they'll take you
on a tour of the stars' homes.

2874
01:30:48,467 --> 01:30:51,067
- But Max, you're
not leaving, are you?

2875
01:30:51,067 --> 01:30:52,800
- [Tom] Uh, sorry, I'm in
love with a union organizer.

2876
01:30:52,800 --> 01:30:55,000
- Everything'll be
back to normal again.

2877
01:30:55,000 --> 01:30:57,700
I mean, it's like, if I can
figure out what's normal again,

2878
01:30:57,700 --> 01:30:59,033
but listen, we could
spend time together.

2879
01:30:59,033 --> 01:31:00,667
I mean, without
bullets flying around

2880
01:31:00,667 --> 01:31:02,467
and helicopters
landing in my backyard.

2881
01:31:02,467 --> 01:31:03,300
- [Max] Alicia?

2882
01:31:03,300 --> 01:31:04,233
- [Tom] Shut up!

2883
01:31:04,233 --> 01:31:05,367
- Is that 10 sentences, yet?

2884
01:31:05,367 --> 01:31:06,200
- What?

2885
01:31:08,867 --> 01:31:11,433
- Oh, you taste just
like Monte Markham.

2886
01:31:11,433 --> 01:31:12,967
- [Joel] You taste like ninja.

2887
01:31:12,967 --> 01:31:15,800
- Don't you be a stranger, okay?

2888
01:31:15,800 --> 01:31:17,267
- I'll remember that.

2889
01:31:17,267 --> 01:31:19,100
- [Tom] This guy's breaking
hearts all over the map.

2890
01:31:19,100 --> 01:31:19,933
- Bye.

2891
01:31:19,933 --> 01:31:21,033
- Bye, Max.

2892
01:31:21,033 --> 01:31:22,000
- [Tom] Bye.

2893
01:31:22,000 --> 01:31:23,600
- [Joel] All right.

2894
01:31:23,600 --> 01:31:24,933
First base, huh?

2895
01:31:26,067 --> 01:31:26,900
- You were right.

2896
01:31:26,900 --> 01:31:28,000
When in doubt--

2897
01:31:28,000 --> 01:31:29,267
- You kiss them.

2898
01:31:29,267 --> 01:31:31,533
- Yeah, hot, I'm a bad
Van Patten, aren't I?

2899
01:31:31,533 --> 01:31:34,500
- Well, we will, as
soon as Okasa's stopped.

2900
01:31:34,500 --> 01:31:36,867
- Well, at least he
wasn't around this time.

2901
01:31:36,867 --> 01:31:38,300
Count our blessings, right?

2902
01:31:38,300 --> 01:31:39,867
- Geez, you need the
universal translator

2903
01:31:39,867 --> 01:31:41,100
to understand that guy.

2904
01:31:41,100 --> 01:31:42,467
- [Joel] Colonel Pressings?

2905
01:31:42,467 --> 01:31:43,933
- Before we go on searching
for your daughter,

2906
01:31:43,933 --> 01:31:45,033
we're going to swing by
Vegas for a little R and R.

2907
01:31:45,033 --> 01:31:47,200
- [Joel] Go stand by Vegas?

2908
01:31:47,200 --> 01:31:49,433
- I thought we just
had a good time.

2909
01:31:49,433 --> 01:31:50,900
- [Tom] D'oh!

2910
01:31:50,900 --> 01:31:54,333
- [Joel] Oh, Master Ninja,
will you ever learn?

2911
01:31:54,333 --> 01:31:56,067
(laughing)

2912
01:31:56,067 --> 01:31:57,733
Well, let's get going.
- [Tom] I'm going to stay.

2913
01:31:57,733 --> 01:31:58,767
- I liked that one.

2914
01:31:58,767 --> 01:32:00,367
- [Tom] Sing the
theme song here.

2915
01:32:00,367 --> 01:32:03,333
(imitating music)

2916
01:32:03,333 --> 01:32:06,533
♪ He's a man with a plan ♪

2917
01:32:06,533 --> 01:32:08,633
♪ He's a ninja ♪

2918
01:32:08,633 --> 01:32:10,167
♪ Hey, oh ♪

2919
01:32:10,167 --> 01:32:15,167
♪ You've got to go
where the hamster goes ♪

2920
01:32:15,933 --> 01:32:17,100
♪ You're a ninja ♪

2921
01:32:17,100 --> 01:32:18,833
Uh, Joel, Joel, Joel!

2922
01:32:19,733 --> 01:32:21,000
Carry me.

2923
01:32:21,000 --> 01:32:22,367
- [Joel] What, are
you sick of this?

2924
01:32:22,367 --> 01:32:25,833
♪ He's got thighs
like a hamster ♪

2925
01:32:25,833 --> 01:32:27,067
♪ Hoo, ah, get down ♪

2926
01:32:27,067 --> 01:32:31,233
♪ Get down, jump
back, kiss myself ♪

2927
01:32:44,733 --> 01:32:46,900
(humming)

2928
01:32:48,000 --> 01:32:49,467
- You know, today's
experiment was

2929
01:32:49,467 --> 01:32:50,833
packed with more Timothy
Van Patten scenes than ever.

2930
01:32:50,833 --> 01:32:53,367
And yet, I feel so empty.

2931
01:32:53,367 --> 01:32:55,600
- Yeah, usually, when I watch
two back-to-back episodes

2932
01:32:55,600 --> 01:32:57,300
of a failed mif-'80s
action show,

2933
01:32:57,300 --> 01:32:59,400
repackaged and presented
as a feature-length movie,

2934
01:32:59,400 --> 01:33:00,733
I expect more.

2935
01:33:00,733 --> 01:33:02,400
- Well, you've got to
admit, the experiments

2936
01:33:02,400 --> 01:33:04,133
have been pretty rugged lately.

2937
01:33:04,133 --> 01:33:08,800
But let's let bygones be bygones
and has-beens be has-beens,

2938
01:33:08,800 --> 01:33:10,167
and have some fun with

2939
01:33:10,167 --> 01:33:13,733
this neat Lee Van Cleef
foamcore dress-up doll.

2940
01:33:13,733 --> 01:33:15,233
You see?

2941
01:33:15,233 --> 01:33:17,867
Lookitk, Lee's already dressed
for action in his Joe Namath

2942
01:33:17,867 --> 01:33:19,967
netted slingshot briefs there.

2943
01:33:19,967 --> 01:33:21,200
- Oh my God, Joel.

2944
01:33:21,200 --> 01:33:22,700
For Heaven's sake, put
some clothes on him.

2945
01:33:22,700 --> 01:33:25,000
- You know, with that gut,
wouldn't the Charles Durning

2946
01:33:25,000 --> 01:33:26,633
underoos be far
more appropriate?

2947
01:33:26,633 --> 01:33:27,467
- Well, no.

2948
01:33:27,467 --> 01:33:29,000
Check it out.

2949
01:33:29,000 --> 01:33:30,500
See what happens when you
put the ninja costume on?

2950
01:33:30,500 --> 01:33:33,133
How, uh, what a slimming
effect it has on the guy?

2951
01:33:33,133 --> 01:33:33,967
- Wow.

2952
01:33:33,967 --> 01:33:35,233
- See, isn't that neat?

2953
01:33:35,233 --> 01:33:36,567
- Hey, could you put a
pirate costume on him?

2954
01:33:36,567 --> 01:33:37,800
- What?

2955
01:33:37,800 --> 01:33:38,900
- Lee Van Cleef didn't
wear a pirate outfit

2956
01:33:38,900 --> 01:33:40,433
in this or any other film.

2957
01:33:40,433 --> 01:33:41,633
- I know.

2958
01:33:41,633 --> 01:33:42,867
It's just a fantasy
I've always had.

2959
01:33:42,867 --> 01:33:44,433
- Anyway, it's time
to read a letter.

2960
01:33:44,433 --> 01:33:45,900
- Oh!

2961
01:33:45,900 --> 01:33:47,333
- Let's put that up on
still store there, Cambot.

2962
01:33:47,333 --> 01:33:48,967
This one comes
from Sue Schroeder

2963
01:33:48,967 --> 01:33:49,800
of Rochester, New York.

2964
01:33:49,800 --> 01:33:50,633
- Hi, Sue.

2965
01:33:50,633 --> 01:33:52,000
- And Sue writes,

2966
01:33:52,000 --> 01:33:53,967
"I can certainly sympathize
with being forced

2967
01:33:53,967 --> 01:33:55,233
"to watch bad movies,

2968
01:33:55,233 --> 01:33:57,300
"because I am a Film
Studies grad student.

2969
01:33:57,300 --> 01:33:59,467
"Most of the movies that
I have to watch, though,

2970
01:33:59,467 --> 01:34:01,633
"are 10 hours long,
and have subtitles.

2971
01:34:01,633 --> 01:34:04,067
"Actually, when I was
still taking classes,

2972
01:34:04,067 --> 01:34:05,933
"I didn't even
get to see movies.

2973
01:34:05,933 --> 01:34:08,200
"All I did was read Freud
and dumb French people

2974
01:34:08,200 --> 01:34:10,000
"like," uh, what's that word?

2975
01:34:10,000 --> 01:34:10,833
- Derrida.

2976
01:34:10,833 --> 01:34:11,667
- "Derrida."

2977
01:34:11,667 --> 01:34:12,500
- Foucault!

2978
01:34:12,500 --> 01:34:13,967
- "I hated it.

2979
01:34:13,967 --> 01:34:16,233
"Well, I almost have my degree,
so it will all be over soon.

2980
01:34:16,233 --> 01:34:18,633
"PS, I want to draw a
picture for you all,

2981
01:34:18,633 --> 01:34:20,733
"but I have to get back
to writing my thesis.

2982
01:34:20,733 --> 01:34:23,467
"Also, will you three say
what your favorite movies

2983
01:34:23,467 --> 01:34:24,867
"of all time are?"

2984
01:34:24,867 --> 01:34:26,267
That's a good one.
- Well, for me it's easy.

2985
01:34:26,267 --> 01:34:27,167
Big Fauss and Little Halsey.

2986
01:34:27,167 --> 01:34:28,000
- Crow?

2987
01:34:28,000 --> 01:34:29,233
- Kafka's The Castle.

2988
01:34:29,233 --> 01:34:30,633
- I thought it was Zardoz.

2989
01:34:30,633 --> 01:34:32,933
- I'd have to say Colossus:
the Forbin Project.

2990
01:34:32,933 --> 01:34:33,867
- Huh.

2991
01:34:33,867 --> 01:34:35,167
- What do you think, sirs?

2992
01:34:35,167 --> 01:34:36,667
- Ah, The Forbin Project.

2993
01:34:36,667 --> 01:34:37,833
One of my favorite films.

2994
01:34:37,833 --> 01:34:39,333
The thing I like most about it--

2995
01:34:39,333 --> 01:34:41,700
- Doctor, can I
just say something?

2996
01:34:41,700 --> 01:34:43,000
Can I just get serious?

2997
01:34:43,000 --> 01:34:44,767
I have something
very important, which

2998
01:34:44,767 --> 01:34:47,300
I really feel has to be said.

2999
01:34:47,300 --> 01:34:48,700
- Well, Frank, you
do look serious.

3000
01:34:48,700 --> 01:34:50,733
Um, by all means,
the floor is yours.

3001
01:34:50,733 --> 01:34:51,967
- Thank you, doctor.

3002
01:34:51,967 --> 01:34:54,100
You know, one thing
in today's experiment

3003
01:34:54,100 --> 01:34:57,633
caused great pain to
yours truly, TVs Frank.

3004
01:34:57,633 --> 01:34:59,900
It was the appearance
of Monte Markham

3005
01:34:59,900 --> 01:35:01,233
in the second episode,

3006
01:35:01,233 --> 01:35:03,633
I mean the later half
of today's movie.

3007
01:35:03,633 --> 01:35:07,633
Monty Markham was the star of
my favorite television series

3008
01:35:07,633 --> 01:35:11,100
when I was just a young man,
living in my mother's basement.

3009
01:35:11,100 --> 01:35:12,700
I'm talking, of course, of

3010
01:35:12,700 --> 01:35:14,733
The Second Hundred Years, which,

3011
01:35:14,733 --> 01:35:18,433
as you all remember, was the
crazy, wild show about him,

3012
01:35:18,433 --> 01:35:22,067
being trapped in suspended
animation for 100 years,

3013
01:35:22,067 --> 01:35:25,300
coming back trying to fit
into contemporary society.

3014
01:35:25,300 --> 01:35:27,067
(laughing)

3015
01:35:27,067 --> 01:35:28,567
I liked it.

3016
01:35:28,567 --> 01:35:31,667
The Second Hundred Years
was truly vintage Markham.

3017
01:35:31,667 --> 01:35:35,733
And I want everyone out there
right now to write to ABC,

3018
01:35:35,733 --> 01:35:39,333
and say, please, please,
Mr. ABC Executive,

3019
01:35:40,800 --> 01:35:44,100
bring back The Second Hundred
Years, starring Monte Markham.

3020
01:35:44,100 --> 01:35:47,400
Please do it for the laughter.

3021
01:35:47,400 --> 01:35:48,467
For the love.

3022
01:35:49,900 --> 01:35:51,000
For the boys.

3023
01:35:53,667 --> 01:35:56,433
- Well, Frank, that
was very touching.

3024
01:35:56,433 --> 01:35:59,100
I'm sure the Second Hundred Year

3025
01:35:59,100 --> 01:36:01,533
issue was on everyone's mind.

3026
01:36:04,500 --> 01:36:07,500
Shall I crush your skull,
or do you want to do it?

3027
01:36:07,500 --> 01:36:09,033
- Oh, I think you ought to.

3028
01:36:09,033 --> 01:36:10,033
- Very well.

3029
01:36:13,333 --> 01:36:15,667
(clanging)

3030
01:36:15,667 --> 01:36:18,633
Well, in the immortal
words of Monte Markham,

3031
01:36:18,633 --> 01:36:21,200
"Here come de judge."

3032
01:36:21,200 --> 01:36:22,867
- [Frank] Uh, that
was Pigmeat Markham.

3033
01:36:22,867 --> 01:36:23,700
(clanging)

3034
01:36:23,700 --> 01:36:24,633
(screaming)

3035
01:36:24,633 --> 01:36:27,633
(light synth music)
